msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Glossary.cs:57
msgid "One thing a chest's last owner hid with a ward: it never sounds, weighs nothing and isn't counted. It comes out only if your slip names it: mark one more of its kind than you heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Glossary.cs:59
msgid "A hidden compartment under the chest's floor. Dropped from high up, the chest lands with a hollow boom. What's under it always comes out; mark the false bottom on your slip for a perfect read."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Glossary.cs:61
msgid "A seller who haggles takes an offer: pick your price on the slider. They take it, come part of the way down, or walk out if you go too low."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Glossary.cs:63
msgid "Nothing of that kind comes out worse than its chest promised."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Glossary.cs:68 scripts/Core/Glossary.cs:102 scripts/Core/Offers.cs:69
#: scripts/Ui/NotebookView.cs:438 scripts/Ui/NotebookView.cs:579 scripts/Ui/NotebookView.cs:657
#: scripts/Ui/NotebookView.cs:705 scripts/Ui/UiKit.cs:336
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0}: {1}"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:63
msgid "Mister Vane"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:68
msgid "Good evening. The Guild's tithe, if you please. In gold: the Guild has no use for promises."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:69
msgid "Still here, I see. Good. The Guild hates to see a Keywright go to waste."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:70
msgid "My masters have begun to ask about you. That is rarely good news. One more week after this one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:71
msgid "The last of Bram's debt. Every coin of it, mind. Gold you can see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:76
msgid "Debts are curious things, Keywright. They grow while nobody's watching them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:77
msgid "The Gate is hungry this week, and the Guild has decided you owe it something for its patience."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:78
msgid "Interest, you understand. Nothing personal. My master is very fond of interest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:85
msgid "Paid in full. The Guild has no further claim on Bram's stall. For now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:86
msgid "Paid. Until next week, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:87
msgid "Paid, and promptly. Until next week, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:90
msgid "Short? Then the Guild will take what's on your shelf instead. At the Guild's price, naturally."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:93
msgid "Not enough. The Guild seals this shop tonight, and your licence with it. Your uncle will be so disappointed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:94
msgid "Not enough. The Guild seals this shop tonight, and your licence with it. Bram will be so disappointed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:97
msgid "A Guild note, older than the Locking? ...However did you come by that? The Guild honours its own paper. Paid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:100
msgid "All of it, tonight? ...How very thorough of you. The Guild has no further claim on Bram's stall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Guild.cs:103
msgid "Bram's word? How touching. One week, then. The rest comes due next week, and half as much again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:82
msgid "The Lullaby Box"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:82
msgid "plink"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:82
msgid "a farmer's wife at Brindle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:83
msgid "She gave the music box that sang her children to sleep. It still plays her lullaby, for a Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:84
msgid "Calms every seller: nobody hurries you or minds what you do with their chest, and all ask a fifth less."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:85
msgid "The Shepherd's Pipe"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:85
msgid "toodle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:85
msgid "a shepherd of the Brindle hills"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:86
msgid "He gave the pipe whose tune could call any flock home. It still calls."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:87
msgid "Calls folk to your door: two more customers a day, and anyone who walks out comes back at their first price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:88
msgid "The Fey Chimes"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:88
msgid "ting"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:88
msgid "the fair folk of the Old Wood"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:89
msgid "They gave the chimes from over their door between the worlds. Where they ring, luck turns."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:90
msgid "Fey luck: a third of what comes out as its chest promised comes out a step better."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:91
msgid "The Dragon's Egg"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:91
msgid "thump"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:91
msgid "Ysolt, the last dragon of the Ember Peaks"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:92
msgid "She gave her egg, still warm. Three hundred years on, its heart still beats."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:93
msgid "Dragon-gold: coin and gems you sell fetch twice their worth."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:94
msgid "The Clockwork Lark"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:94
msgid "tweet"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:94
msgid "a tinker of Crownhold"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:95
msgid "He gave the bird he built for a princess who never woke. It sings at dawn, and carries word."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:96
msgid "Carries word across Aldmark: two more commissions a week, and every commission pays half as much again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:97
msgid "The Hearthstone"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:97
msgid "hummm"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:97
msgid "the dwarves of Ironroot"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:98
msgid "They gave a stone from their first hearth. It hums with three thousand years of warm evenings."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:99
#, csharp-format
msgid "Folk come for miles to sit by it: {0}g a night for each point of exhibition (more in a grander shop)."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:100 scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:18
msgid "The Drowned Bell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:100
msgid "dong"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:100
msgid "old Aldwater, before the river took it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:101
msgid "The town gave its chapel bell, which rang the hours for every soul in Aldwater. It still counts, under the water."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:102
msgid "It counts for you: as a chest comes to the counter, it tolls once for each thing inside, false bottom and all."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:103
msgid "The Bottled Star"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:103
msgid "twinkle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:103
msgid "the archmages of the Keyhold"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:104
msgid "They gave a star they caught as students and kept in a bottle all their lives. Things from the Locking gather round it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:105
msgid "Starlight: enchanted things glow whenever they sound, witchlight or not, and turn up far more often."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:106
msgid "The Imp's Ember"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:106
msgid "crackle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:106
msgid "Pib, an imp who loved a miller's daughter"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:107
msgid "He gave his own heart, a coal that never goes out, so the Maw could never have her."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:108
msgid "Tempers all it warms: glass never breaks, nothing comes out worse than promised, and fakes you open burn true."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:116
msgid "A lock of gold could never hold the demon of greed. So at the Locking the archmages asked the peoples of Aldmark for things they loved more than gold, and sang the Locking into nine of them: the Heartsongs. Then they hid each in an ordinary chest, among millions. Only a Keywright hears one sing. To anyone else it's worth nothing, and the Guild won't touch one: greed can't put a price on it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:12
msgid "Uncle Bram"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:12
msgid "Bram"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:20
msgid "Morning! Here's the trick of it: a chest opens for you once you've paid for it, and nobody can see inside, so everyone shakes it and guesses. Pip never even shook his. Drag the chest slowly from side to side: that's a gentle shake."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:23
msgid "Your back won't take a hard shake or a drop, Hesk, but your scale doesn't lie. Weigh what you heard against what's on the scale: whatever's left over is something you couldn't hear, or something under a false bottom."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:25
msgid "Everybody haggles with you, Rosa, though they open a bit higher, knowing you. Make your offer with the slider. Too low and they'll let you try again, but walk one out of the door and they won't be back this week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:27
#, csharp-format
msgid "Your shelf's up from the first day, Isolde. Keep what you love: visitors pay at the door every night, {0}g for every {1} points of exhibition. Just remember the Guild won't take your collection in pawn on a short night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:29
msgid "Hear that jingle? Coin. Light things rattle at the gentlest shake. Tick Coin on your slip, there on the right."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:30
msgid "Your slip adds up what you've ticked, valued as good as the chest's colour promises. The bar underneath is your odds that it's worth more than the price: the greener, the safer."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:32
msgid "Ada only shook it gently. Nothing heavy or soft stirs for a gentle shake, so she's priced only what she heard. Try every strength yourself: gentle, firm and hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:34
msgid "That flump is a cloak. Soft things only make a sound when you shake hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:35
msgid "Garrick shook it hard, and when something clanks, it drowns out anything delicate. Shake it yourself, at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:36
msgid "Clank: a weapon, an axe or a blade. It only moves when you shake firmly, and while it's clanking you can't hear anything delicate. Shake gently to hear past it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:38
msgid "Bettany counts the rattles at a firm shake and charges the same for each. If you can't hear anything she didn't, pass: a seller always asks a bit more than what they've heard is worth."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:40
msgid "When you pass, they take it home unopened, and you'll never know for sure. But your gut usually has an opinion."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:41
msgid "Your mark went cold: that chest isn't theirs to sell, and it won't open for whoever buys it. Pass on it, or send for the Wardens: they pay a finder's share."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:43
msgid "Not everyone comes to sell. People have their own troubles, and what you say to them comes back: who comes, what they bring, and who's on your side. The notebook's Town page keeps track."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:45
msgid "The best tools aren't sold in shops: the people who make them bring them to the counter. Say no, and they'll ask again in a few days."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:47
msgid "A tick is a good read. A cross is something to listen for next time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:48
msgid "You bought that one sight unseen, so there was nothing to read: a closed eye is a thing you never marked, not a mistake. Handle a chest before you buy it and your slip is checked as usual."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:50
msgid "A closed eye is a thing you never listened for: you never shook the chest at the strength that stirs it, or never dropped it for what's under the floor. A cross is for what you listened to and got wrong. Gently, firmly, hard: every strength tells you something the others can't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:52
msgid "That's a day's trading. A week of them here, then Thornwick Market, a step further in: richer chests, and dearer ones. So let the purse grow."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:55
msgid "Look at the chest's colour: plain wood, green, blue, purple. The Wardens painted them by what went in, so the colour tells you how good the things inside tend to be. Only tend to: you'll get surprises both ways."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:57
msgid "See? Not everything matches its chest. Mostly it does; sometimes it's a little worse; now and then it's much better."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:58
msgid "This one names a price. Take it or leave it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:59
msgid "This one haggles, so they'll start high. Use the slider to make one offer: they'll take it, name a final price, or storm off if you insult them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:61
msgid "This one wants you to name a price. Offer what it's worth to you, less a little. You get two tries."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:62
msgid "Too low. One more try, then they'll go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:63
msgid "Everyone you've traded with has a page in your notebook: how they judge a chest, how they trade, what they're like. Click whoever's at the counter to read theirs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:65
msgid "Missed what someone said? My old echo horn, at the end of the counter, keeps every word said across it. Click it to hear the lot again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:67
msgid "Listen to where they say it came from. A barrow holds grave goods, a goblin warren mostly coin, a dwarf-hold weapons and gems."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:69
msgid "Something grand? You can keep it for display instead of selling it. A good exhibition brings more customers, and better ones. Enchanted things count double."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:71
msgid "On display. You'll see it on the shelf behind the counter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:72
msgid "Your exhibition. Click anything in it to sell it, if you need the money."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:75
msgid "A proper shop, with room to grow: this is where you spend on it, and the people who make the best tools will bring them to the counter. Chests cost more here, so keep enough for tomorrow's. A price in red means it would leave you short: better to wait a day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:76
msgid "Nearly broke? I keep a little put by for days like this. Don't tell the Guild. It won't last forever: the day card says how much is left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:78
msgid "A shelf behind the counter, with room for one thing! Keep something grand on display instead of selling it: an exhibition draws more customers, and better chests. Each cabinet you buy makes room for one more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:80
#, csharp-format
msgid "Crownhold folk know a shop by what it collects. Your notebook has tallied everything you've acquired: {0} of a kind earns a synergy. Open Synergies, bottom right, to put one to work or see how close you are."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:81
msgid "Another synergy slot: open Synergies and put one more to work."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:82
msgid "The Royal Emporium, in the palace's shadow. The Gate's just down the street: you can feel it hum. There are bigger things to grow into now: a night market, a patrons' book, a velvet case for curios. Keep enough back for Vane."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:84
msgid "Forgotten a sound, or someone's habits? Press N for your notebook: the sounds, the regulars you've met, and a calendar of what's coming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:86
msgid "That's the Guild's next due, up top. Click it any time for the whole debt in your notebook: what's paid, what's left, and what each week will want."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:88
msgid "The chest is yours. Now for its old lock. The pick sweeps round: press {act}, or click, while it's in the green to set a pin; each pin you set sends it back the other way. Set every pin cleanly and nothing inside gets scratched."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:92
msgid "Paid. Next week the Guild wants more, and more again the week after. Whatever you spend on the shop has to earn its keep before Vane comes back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:94
msgid "That curio pays on chests bought sight unseen: bought without shaking, dropping or putting the lodestone to them. The witchlight's fine. A '?' on a card means it uses a word like that: hover over it to read it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:96
msgid "Bram's word is me vouching for you on a Guild night you can't pay: the Guild takes all your gold, and what's still owed, half as much again, goes on next week's due. Once a run, and never in the last week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:98
msgid "Nim comes every night after closing with curios: oddments from the Locking, each bending one rule of the trade. One a night at first; his lantern brings more. Pick ones that work together: Nim notices what you buy and brings more like it. Don't ask what Nim is."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:101
msgid "The regulars want things now: see the board on the left. When something they want comes out of a chest, hand it over instead of selling it. A commission always pays more than a sale, and a lot pays piece by piece."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:103
msgid "Someone wants this! Deliver it: a commission always pays more than selling it would."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:104
msgid "Something's happening in town today: two days every week are different. It's up in the top bar (click it to read it again), and your notebook's calendar shows what's coming this week and next."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:106
msgid "The Stranger. That chest's wrapped in iron chains: nothing inside can move, so there's nothing to hear. Drop it to feel how heavy it is. Heavy ones hold more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:108
msgid "A royal seal! That's one of King Aldric's own chests, gilded. The seller thinks the gold is paint, and priced it as the colour underneath."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:110
msgid "Look at that purse: enough to pay off the whole back-tithe, every week of it, right now! Do it, and the stall is ours early. Or keep trading first: the Guild only ever asks for this week's."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:112
msgid "Short? Pawn what's on display, or your curios, at the Guild's price. If even that isn't enough, the Guild seals the shop."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:113
msgid "Short, and folk owe you a favour? Call on them first: each brings an eighth of the due, once a season. That's what friends are for."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:114
msgid "Gold! A legend, that. They're made, not mended: no restorer or lucky charm will ever turn a thing gold. It went into that chest gold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:117
msgid "Thornwick folk bring two new sounds. Potions slosh at a gentle shake, like coin. Spells (scrolls and spellbooks) rustle only at a hard shake, like cloaks. And some chests are locked, or have a false bottom. It'll be a quiet first day, while word gets round."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:120
msgid "Locked. Buy it and you'll pick the lock before you open it. A crowbar's quicker, but it breaks glass."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:121
msgid "Dropped! A solid thud means a plain chest. A hollow boom means a false bottom: something hidden that nobody's priced."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:122
msgid "Hear that boom? A false bottom. Tick it on your slip: whatever's down there, nobody's priced it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:123
msgid "Glass breaks when you drop it. If you heard a slosh, think twice before dropping."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:124
msgid "That slosh is a potion. It's delicate, like coin: a clank drowns it out."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:125
msgid "A rustle: a spell, a scroll or a spellbook. Soft, like a cloak: it only sounds at a hard shake."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:126
msgid "Crownhold brings gems, which tinkle at a gentle shake; archmages, whose things are often enchanted (a witchlight would show it); and lots with two or three of a kind. Count the rattles: click a row again for each one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:128
msgid "A tinkle: a gem. Delicate, and worth the most."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:129
msgid "The witchlight's lit, and it stays lit: anything enchanted glows when it makes a sound. Click the star on a row to mark one enchanted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:131
msgid "Two of a kind: each one adds its value. Sellers who don't count only price one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:132
msgid "It glowed! That one's enchanted, and worth twice as much. Click the star on its row to mark it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:134
msgid "The Lantern Market's open under the Barrow tonight, and Nim will take you down. His people sell what can't be bought by daylight, and buy what nobody else will. Mind who you sell gold to down there."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:137
msgid "A mimic! It's eaten whatever was in there. The Arcanum's menagerie pays well for one. Or keep it: it eats gold on Guild nights, no thief tries a door with a mimic behind it, and once it's eaten its fill it sleeps on the gold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:139
msgid "Hush. Hear that? Something in there is breathing. Where the Locking frays, an old ward goes hungry and eats what's in its chest: a mimic. Nothing rattles, so the seller thinks it's empty. The Arcanum's menagerie pays well for one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:141
msgid "The Royal Emporium. Court folk, the Maw's creatures up through the cracks in the Gate, and Gilt, who sells demon gold: gilded iron that jingles just like the real thing. A lodestone would catch it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:143
msgid "The lodestone's on, so iron can't move. Weapons go quiet, and nothing drowns out the delicate things. Demon gold, which is iron under the gilt, goes quiet too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:145
msgid "That's all the shaking this one will stand: it's coming apart. Go by what you heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:148
msgid "That sound... I've heard it once in forty years. A Heartsong! Only a Keywright hears one sing, so the seller has no idea it's there. It's worth nothing in gold and everything to the shop: buy that chest. And if you can't afford it, pass: a Heartsong won't leave with them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:151
msgid "A Heartsong. Nobody would pay a penny for one, but each does something for the shop that no gold can, for as long as it sings here. Keep it or let it go: every one you keep makes the next harder to find."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:153
msgid "Hear that? The whole stall's different with it singing. It'll sing as long as it's ours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:154
msgid "One more thing. Somewhere among all these chests are nine Heartsongs: things loved so much they sing. Only a Keywright hears them, at the gentlest shake. Most seasons never hear one. If you ever do, buy that chest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:159
msgid "Ada only shakes gently, so heavy things and soft things make no sound for her."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:160
msgid "Tobin's Barrow chests are rotten: about two seconds of shaking, all told. One strength, then: pick it well."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:161
msgid "Nettle puts her price up a tenth for every strength you try after the first. Pick two: gentle and hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:162
msgid "Mother Sorrel always dreams true, in signs. If you can't hear what she dreamt of, it's warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:163
msgid "A Thornwick dowry always holds coin, a cloak and a potion. Whichever of the three you can't hear is warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:164
msgid "Ilse's tag lists every kind of thing packed. A kind on the tag that never makes a sound is warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:165
msgid "Quire's ward-roll names the warded thing, faded. Make out the name, and tick its kind."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:166
msgid "Madame Zell's cards: a suit drawn twice is what the ward holds. Three different suits, and nothing's warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:167
msgid "A warded thing makes no sound and weighs nothing. Name it on your slip, and nothing that isn't there, and the ward will give it up."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:169
msgid "You could pay off the Guild now. Or buy its Bookkeeping Engine for the same sum: it reads every chest for you, to finish the run quickly."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:171
msgid "Rook's scale says what her chest weighs. Take away the weight of what you heard: what's left never stirred (a cloak is 3 lb, a spell 1)."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:173
msgid "Brass's ticket counts every article, false bottom and all. Count what you hear: one short means one under the floor."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:174
msgid "Flick's chests are mostly stolen. Lay a hand on each one: if your mark goes cold, send for the Wardens, or pass."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:176
msgid "The Guild's bailiff, selling what it took for tithe to its friends: cheap, by the colour alone. But a lot of what the Guild takes was never the Guild's to sell. Lay a hand on every one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:178
msgid "The Wardens' quartermaster sells what nobody claimed, by the pound. A heavy chest comes dear and a light one cheap: take the weight of what you hear from his scale's."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:180
msgid "Brother Cadoc won't have his chests shaken hard: half again if you do. Crypt chests are full of holy cloaks."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:181
msgid "Corvin packs his chests in straw: everything needs a strength harder to stir, and cloaks and spells won't stir at all. Shake firmly, then hard, then drop it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:183
msgid "Orme likes a wager: read her chest exactly, every kind and every count, and she gives back a third of the price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:184
msgid "Solve grandmother's riddle. If you can't hear what it's about, it's warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:185
msgid "Sir Rowan takes the best weapon in his chest, for the fee he names. Value what's left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:186
msgid "Tick gives you twelve seconds. Gently, then hard, and decide."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:187
msgid "Sallow is cheap, but the dearest thing inside is his. A chest of many middling things suits his bargain."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:188
msgid "Skrae's echoes come back off everything, warded or not. An echo with nothing to hear is warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:189
msgid "Countess Vey prices only her gems; the rest comes free. Some are paste, and she won't have a lodestone near them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:190
msgid "Old Aldo's price is your slip. Get it exactly right and he takes a quarter off; get it wrong and you pay what it holds, and a quarter more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:192
msgid "The Maw sells for one coin, but everyone who comes after him today asks twice as much. Count who's still waiting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:41
msgid "Where is Bram?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:42
msgid "What was the breathing chest?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:43
msgid "Why did the first morning come again?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:44
msgid "How do we bring them out?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:56
msgid "\"The Guild's treasury has asked for Bram. An old consignment needs his attention. Temporary work.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:57
msgid "\"Keep the shop running until he returns, and his account paid. Earn the treasury key, and bring it to the treasury on the season's last night.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:58
msgid "Bram said he'd write every week. No letter has come from him. The Guild's letters come."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:59
msgid "\"The Guild has father's note, due on its first night. If it isn't paid they'll take the yard, and him, to work it off.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:60
msgid "The Guild took Old Haddon on its first night, to work off his note. Nell is minding the yard alone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:61
msgid "You paid Old Haddon's note before the Guild's night. He stayed home, and swore at the Guild from his yard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:62
msgid "Bram's tuning fork, in a lot of the Guild's repossessed goods. Its tag: from the weighhouse, palace road. Not the treasury: the weighhouse."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:63
msgid "\"Guild carts pass my toll every fifth night, under sacking, down the palace road. A sack slipped once. It was a man. A gold man.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:64
msgid "Follow a Guild cart from Thornwick's toll, on a Guild night. (Or buy a night at the weighhouse at the Lantern Market.)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:66
msgid "Under the palace road, the Guild's weighhouse: crates in rows, each chalked with a name and a weight. \"H. Haddon, 14 stone.\" \"Bram, keywright, 13 stone.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:67
msgid "A page of the Guild's ledger: \"H. Haddon, fourteen stone, to the weighhouse.\" People, written down by weight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:68
msgid "A copy of the weighhouse register: every crate by name and weight, and the night it goes to the treasury."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:69
msgid "Listen to a Guild crate at the counter: let it sit still, and knock back if it knocks."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:71
msgid "A Guild crate knocked when it sat still. You knocked back, and it answered. The gilded are alive."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:72
msgid "A crate tapped twice, then once: the way Bram taps the counter. He's in there."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:73
msgid "Get Bram's crate off the palace road: Corvin buys what falls off a Guild cart, and the Lantern Market's bargemen will divert one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:75
msgid "Get Bram's crate off the palace road: with Corvin gone, the Lantern Market's bargemen are the way. They'll divert one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:77
msgid "Free whoever's in the back room: a full mimic eats the gold off them, and their note must be redeemed or they'll be taken again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:83
msgid "\"Twenty years ago the Mark-Finders came for you: a marked baby. I pledged them my hand, mark and all. That was my account.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:84
msgid "\"Twenty years ago the Mark-Finders came for a marked baby, my niece Kit. I pledged them my hand, mark and all. That was my account.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:86
msgid "Bram came home, cold to the bone, and sat by the stove, and laughed at nothing for an hour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:89
msgid "The treasury's chest didn't sound. It didn't ring, not even the way an empty chest rings. It slipped, and it breathed. Then it opened."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:90
msgid "A chest at the counter breathed while it sat still. Opened, it was a mimic: a chest that had eaten what was in it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:91
msgid "Listen for a chest that breathes while it sits still. From Thornwick, one turns up now and then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:93
msgid "Keep a mimic in the back room and feed it on Guild nights, or leave it with the Arcanum's menagerie."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:95
msgid "Fed twice, the mimic ate its fill and fell asleep on the gold. Wanting something isn't wanting everything."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:96
msgid "A full mimic ate the gold off someone the Guild had taken, and they stepped out of it, cold. Their note still stood: the Guild could take them again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:97
msgid "\"Before there were Locking chests there was one chest. It was empty, and it wanted. We didn't invent the Locking, Keywright. We copied it.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:100
msgid "You woke on the first morning. Bram tapped the counter, twice and once. He doesn't remember any of it. You do."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:101
msgid "\"We've met before, I think. You always look at my ring like that.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:102
msgid "\"The Keyhold gave the seal a last clause: if the Maw breaks out without leave, the year turns back to its first morning. Whoever touched the seal remembers. So does he.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:103
msgid "Someone at Crownhold knows what the Keyhold put in the seal. Find the hooded woman."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:105
msgid "A stolen chest you sent home opened for its owner the moment she touched it. Paying for a chest doesn't make it yours: the ward decides."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:106
msgid "Find out what the Crown actually pledged: Master Quire keeps the Chest Roll at Crownhold, and the King keeps the charter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Inquiry.cs:108
msgid "The treasury's charter: the Crown pledged its keys and its takings to the Guild. Not its people. Not a keywright's word."
msgstr ""

