#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:379
msgid "Rafe carried this through two wars. {price} would help my Jory."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:380
msgid "From the attic, dear, under Rafe's old saddle. {price}? Every coin's for Jory."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:381
msgid "A soldier's widow selling her husband's things to free her son from the Guild's debt-house. She only ever shakes a chest gently, so what's heavy (a weapon) or soft (a cloak) never makes a sound for her, and she doesn't price it. A soldier's kitbag usually holds both."
