msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:448
msgid "Burrow chest. Smells of goblin. Is fine. {price}, and more every time you shake it different."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:449
msgid "Ooh, you like! Price go up: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:449
msgid "More shaking, more gold! {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:449
msgid "Hehe. {price} now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:450
msgid "A goblin of the hills, trading chests out of her clan's burrow (fairly: she'll tell you so). She only shakes gently, so she never prices what a gentle shake can't stir, and goblins charge for everything, looking included: each strength you try after your first puts her price up a tenth."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:453
msgid "Shiny! Shiny!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:453
msgid "Hehehe. Nettle's burrow gets a door!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:454
msgid "Pah! Nettle has other customers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:455
msgid "Pah! Nettle sell it to someone with eyes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:455
msgid "Your loss. Nettle's gain. Nettle always gains."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:456
msgid "Eek! Nettle's chest!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:456
msgid "Hehe, again! Again!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:457
msgid "You drop Nettle's chest? Price go up!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:461
msgid "Rook Varga"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:461
msgid "Rook"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:464
msgid "The Magpie's bounty, the biggest the Wardens have ever posted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:465
msgid "Draws her bow left-handed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:465
msgid "A hunter's clean hands: no ink."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:465
msgid "Rides in boots."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:467
msgid "Took it off an outlaws' camp on the forest road, for the Wardens' bounty. My scale says {pounds}. {price}. Gently: the mare spooks."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:468
msgid "The outlaws won't be needing it. {pounds} on my scale, and I price by the pound: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:469
msgid "Found it in a wolf den. The wolves had eaten whoever was carrying it. {pounds} on my scale. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:470
msgid "Wolves don't hoard, but their dinners did. {pounds}, to the half pound. {price}. Easy with it: the mare."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:471
msgid "A huntress who takes the Wardens' bounties, and sells what the outlaws had. She weighs every chest on her game scale and prices it by the pound, so light things (spells, gems) come cheap. Her chests hang on a mare who bolts at a hard shake: take the weight of what you heard from the scale's, and what's left is what never stirred."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:474
msgid "Good hunting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:475
msgid "The mare's restless. I'm off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:476
msgid "No matter. It'll sell at the next market."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:476 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:596
msgid "Fair enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:477
msgid "Easy! You'll have the mare bolting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:477 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:597
msgid "Steady."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:478
msgid "Easy! You've upset the mare, and me. Half again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:482
msgid "Mother Sorrel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:482
msgid "Sorrel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:485
msgid "To keep the Guild's axes out of the Old Wood."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:486
msgid "Fingers green from her herbs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:486
msgid "Goes barefoot, always."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:487
msgid "The Old Wood let this one go. I slept beside it and dreamt of {dream}. The oaks whispered its price: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:488
msgid "Moss grew on it for a hundred years. Last night I dreamt of {dream}, and of a price: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:489
msgid "The Old Wood's druid at Thornwick. Her price comes to her in a dream, and she always dreams true, in signs: of what the Wood warded in the chest, or else of the dearest thing in it. A magpie is coin, a thorn a weapon, a raven's wing a cloak, a river a potion, an owl a spell, a star a gem. If you can't hear what she dreamt of, it's warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:492
msgid "As the Wood wills."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:492
msgid "The oaks approve."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:493
msgid "The Wood is calling me home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:494
msgid "The Wood is patient. So am I."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:494
msgid "Then it wasn't meant for you. Not yet."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:495
msgid "Mind the moss, child."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:495
msgid "The Wood felt that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:496
msgid "The Wood felt that, child. So will your purse."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:500
msgid "Brother Cadoc"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:500
msgid "Cadoc"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:502
msgid "Bread for the poor at the abbey gate, and the Unopened kept off its steps."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:503
msgid "From the crypt of Saint Ide, by the Abbot's leave. A firm shake, but not hard, please: the saints are resting. {price}, for the poor."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:504
msgid "A brother's reliquary, three hundred years asleep. {price} feeds the poor at our gate for a week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:505
msgid "The almoner of the abbey of Saint Ide, selling the crypt's chests to feed the poor at its gate. He shakes a chest firmly and won't have it shaken hard (half again if you do), so the holy cloaks a crypt chest is full of never make a sound for him, and go unpriced."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:508
msgid "Bless you. The gate eats tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:508
msgid "Saint Ide thanks you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:509 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:513
msgid "Brother! The saints! Half again, for the sacrilege."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:510
msgid "Forgive me, I'm due at vespers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:511
msgid "Another day, perhaps. The poor are patient. They have to be."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:511
msgid "Peace be with you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:512
msgid "Brother! Gently!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:512
msgid "Oh! Saint Ide preserve us."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:517
msgid "Corvin Tallow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:517
msgid "Corvin"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:520
msgid "One more good season on the smugglers' road, and then a boat, and the sea."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:521
msgid "Packed in straw, so nothing clinked at the Wardens' toll. {price}, and no questions."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:522
msgid "Came up the smugglers' road. Don't ask whose. The straw stays: it muffles everything. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:523
msgid "Runs brandy and chests past the Wardens' toll on the forest road, every chest packed in straw so nothing clinks: everything in it needs a strength harder to stir, and cloaks and spells won't stir at all. A firm shake, never a drop, and smugglers love a false bottom. Haggles. Now and then a chest he carries isn't his to sell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:526
msgid "Pleasure. We never met."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:526
msgid "Done. Mind the Wardens."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:527
msgid "{price}, and you're robbing me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:527
msgid "Tch. {price}, final."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:528
msgid "Hmph. Plenty of other buyers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:528
msgid "I've a wagon to catch."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:529
msgid "Your loss. I was never here."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:529
msgid "Suit yourself. Forget my face."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:530
msgid "Quiet! Do you want the Wardens round?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:530
msgid "Easy. That's straw, not stone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:531
msgid "Quiet, you fool! That noise will cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:535
msgid "Aunt Hesper"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:535
msgid "Hesper"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:538
msgid "To marry off the whole county, and to know whose chests are whose: a matchmaker keeps every family's accounts."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:539
msgid "Ink on her fingers from the marriage contracts."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:539
msgid "Rides her pony in boots, village to village."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:540
msgid "A dowry, love, from a wedding that never was: {clue}, as ever. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:541
msgid "The groom ran off to the Barrow. Her dowry: {clue}. {price}. I've another match for her already."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:542
msgid "Thornwick's matchmaker, selling dowries from weddings that never happened. A Thornwick dowry always holds coin for luck, a cloak for warmth and a potion for health, and a bride often wards one of the three: whichever you can't hear is the warded one. Hesper shakes hard and prices what she hears, never what's warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:545
msgid "May it bring you luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:545
msgid "Mind you use it well, love."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:546
msgid "I've a match to make, love. Toodle-oo."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:547
msgid "Ah well. There's always another wedding."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:547
msgid "Not to your taste? Nor was the groom to hers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:548
msgid "Mind the bride's things, love!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:548
msgid "Ooh! Careful."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:549
msgid "That's a bride's dowry, love! It'll cost you more now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:553 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:553
msgid "Flick"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:556
msgid "To be paid, to be fed, and never to be caught. Runs chests for the Magpie."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:557
msgid "It came my way, didn't it. {price}, quick. I can't stand about, mister."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:558
msgid "Don't ask where it's from and I won't ask what you'll do with it. {price}. Twenty seconds."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:559
msgid "A {colour} chest for {price}. Cheap, 'cause I'm in a hurry. Yes or no?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:560
msgid "A pickpocket of twelve who runs chests for the Magpie: cheap, priced by colour, and in a hurry (twenty seconds). Most of what Flick sells isn't Flick's to sell: lay a hand on it, and your mark goes cold. From Thornwick in, you can send for the Wardens."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:562
msgid "Ta. Never saw you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:562
msgid "Done. I'm off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:563
msgid "Too slow, mister. I'm gone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:564
msgid "Someone'll have it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:565
msgid "Oi! Quiet!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:565
msgid "Careful! People are looking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:566
msgid "Drop it again and the price goes up. And the Wardens come running."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:572
msgid "Bailiff Marrow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:572
msgid "Marrow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:574
msgid "The Guild's books balanced, and its friends served first."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:575
msgid "From a house the Guild sealed for tithe. A {colour} chest at the Guild's book price: {price}. The Guild doesn't haggle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:576
msgid "Taken for tithe, and sold to the Guild's friends first. The book says a {colour} chest is {price}, whatever's in it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:577
msgid "The Gilded Guild's bailiff, who sells what it took for tithe to the Guild's friends first, at its book price: the chest's colour, nothing more. A third of it was seized, not sold, and won't open for anyone: lay a hand on it. He comes while the Guild counts you a friend."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:579
msgid "Entered in the book. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:579
msgid "The Guild thanks its friends."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:580
msgid "I've three more houses to see to today."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:581
msgid "As you like. Someone else is a friend of the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:581 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:698
msgid "Noted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:582
msgid "That's Guild property until it's paid for."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:583
msgid "Damage to Guild property is added to the price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:587
msgid "Quartermaster Brandt"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:587
msgid "Brandt"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:589
msgid "The Wardens' store emptied, and the money in the widows' fund."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:590
msgid "Taken off a thief a year and a day ago, and nobody's claimed it. The Wardens' tariff is by the pound: {pounds}, so {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:591
msgid "Unclaimed, a year and a day: it's the Crown's to sell now. {pounds} on the toll scale, at the tariff: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:592
msgid "The Wardens' quartermaster at the Thornwick toll, selling what they took off thieves and nobody claimed in a year and a day. The Wardens' tariff is so much a pound, so heavy things come dear and light ones cheap. He comes while the Wardens count you a friend."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:594
msgid "For the widows' fund. Much obliged."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:594
msgid "Sold, by the tariff."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:595
msgid "The toll won't keep itself."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:596
msgid "It'll keep. It's kept a year already."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:597
msgid "Easy with the Crown's property."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:598
msgid "That's breakage. Breakage goes on the price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:604
msgid "Ilse Varrow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:604
msgid "Ilse"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:607
msgid "To be an archmage one day. Lately, to know what her mistress is building in the cellar."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:608
msgid "Archmage Orme's clearing out the Arcanum stores. The tag says: packed, {clue}. She says {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:609
msgid "This one's from the third cellar. I can read the tag, at least: {clue}. {price}, my mistress says."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:610
msgid "The Arcanum's apprentice, clearing its stores for her mistress. Every chest still has its packing tag, listing each kind of thing packed in it, and the archmages warded the most dangerous: a kind on the tag that you can't hear is warded. Prices by the chest's colour, as she's told."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:613
msgid "Oh good! Don't tell my mistress I was nervous."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:613
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:614
msgid "I'm late! She'll turn me into something."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:615
msgid "Oh. She won't be pleased."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:615
msgid "That's all right. There's a whole cellar of them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:616
msgid "Careful! Some of those are cursed!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:616
msgid "Eep!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:617
msgid "She said to keep them in one piece! I'll have to ask more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:621
msgid "Archmage Thessaly Orme"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:621
msgid "Orme"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:623
msgid "To understand the Locking well enough to undo it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:624
msgid "From the Arcanum's oldest stores. {price}. Tell me exactly what's in it, and a third comes back to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:625
msgid "A {colour} chest: {price}. Read it true, Keywright, and I'll return a third. I study how your kind hears."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:626
msgid "An archmage of the Arcanum who studies the Locking, and Keywrights. She prices by the chest's colour, and likes a wager: read her chest exactly right, every kind and every count, and she gives back a third of what you paid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:628
msgid "Let us see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:628
msgid "We shall see what you heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:629
msgid "My engine won't build itself. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:630
msgid "Prudent. Or timid. We shall never know."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:630
msgid "Another time, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:631
msgid "Hm. Bold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:631
msgid "Fascinating. Do that again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:632
msgid "That chest is older than your great-grandmother. A third more, I think."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:636
msgid "Durgan Ironhand"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:636
msgid "Durgan"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:638
msgid "Ironroot's crown, locked in the Royal Treasury since the Locking; and a buyer for dwarf-gold the Guild won't let him sell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:639
msgid "From the deep seam under Ironroot. {price}. Not a coin of it to the Guild, mind."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:640
msgid "From Ironroot hold, sealed since my great-great-grandmother's day. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:641
msgid "A dwarf trader of Ironroot Street, who knows a weapon when he hears one. He prices weapons in full, everything else at half, and takes every tinkle for a diamond. He shakes hard, and haggles."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:643
msgid "Done. Back to the deep."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:643
msgid "Ha! Done."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:644
msgid "{price}. Any lower and I'll eat my helmet."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:644
msgid "{price}, and that's stone-solid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:645
msgid "You take me for a fool? Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:646
msgid "Hmph. Your loss, surface-dweller."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:646
msgid "Back down the mine with it, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:647
msgid "Ha! Dwarf-made. It'll take worse than that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:647
msgid "Watch it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:648
msgid "Mind my stone-work! That'll cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:652 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1333
msgid "Lady Isaura Vell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:652
msgid "Isaura"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:655
msgid "To keep the Vell house standing, despite her brother's debts."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:656
msgid "Grandmother's trick box. Her riddle's on the lid: \"{clue}\" {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:657
msgid "From the Vell strongroom, before my brother finds it: {price}. Grandmother's riddle: \"{clue}\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:658
msgid "A noblewoman of an old house gone poor, selling her grandmother's trick boxes before her brother can. Each lid has grandmother's riddle about one thing inside, and if she warded something, the riddle is about that. Solve it: if you can't hear the answer, it's warded. Prices by colour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:661
msgid "How delightful."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:661
msgid "Grandmother would approve."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:662
msgid "I have creditors at four. Do excuse me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:663
msgid "Pity. Grandmother so loved a puzzle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:663
msgid "Another time, perhaps."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:664
msgid "Goodness!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:664
msgid "Do be careful, that's a Vell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:665
msgid "That is a Vell heirloom! The price has just gone up."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:669
msgid "Silas Brass"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:669
msgid "Brass"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:672
msgid "His money; and, though he'll never say it, to be thought kind."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:673
msgid "Pledged twenty years ago on Lantern Lane and never redeemed. The ticket says {articles}. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:674
msgid "Ticket four thousand and twelve: {articles}, it says. I price a lot kind by kind. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:675
msgid "The pawnbroker of Lantern Lane, selling pledges nobody redeemed, often two or three of a kind. He prices one of each kind he hears and never counts how many. The pawn ticket counts every article pledged, false bottom and all, and he won't have pledges dropped: count what you hear against the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:678
msgid "Done. No refunds."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:678
msgid "Sold, as heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:679 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:683
msgid "Not on my pledges! Half again, for the damage."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:680
msgid "Time is money, and you're spending mine."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:681
msgid "Back on the shelf it goes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:681
msgid "As you like. Pledges keep."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:682
msgid "Mind the pledges!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:687
msgid "Master Quire"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:687
msgid "Quire"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:690
msgid "The Chest Roll kept true. Lately, to know why it says the Guild's chests aren't the Guild's."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:691
msgid "From the Royal Archive's vaults, with its ward-roll: {clue}. Unclaimed since the Locking. So much a rattle: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:692
msgid "The Chest Roll lists no owner for this one. The ward-roll reads {clue}, as far as I can make it out. I counted the rattles: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:693
msgid "The Royal Archivist, keeper of the Chest Roll, selling unclaimed vault chests with their ward-rolls. A roll names what was warded in its chest, its letters faded by three hundred years: read the name, and name its kind on your slip. A blank roll means nothing was warded. He counts the rattles at a firm shake and charges the same for each."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:696
msgid "Duly recorded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:696
msgid "I'll enter it in the Roll."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:697
msgid "The Archive closes at six. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:698
msgid "Very well. I'll file it under 'unsold'."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:699
msgid "Careful! That's Crown property."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:699
msgid "Oh dear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:700
msgid "That is Crown property! I'll have to add a fee for that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:704
msgid "Tilly Mudge"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:704
msgid "Tilly"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:707
msgid "To find the bell she hears tolling under the Aldwater on still nights."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:708
msgid "Out of the Aldwater mud at low tide! I'd bet my boots on what rustles. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:709
msgid "The river gives and the river takes. Spellbooks, potions, who knows! {price}. Heard the bell again last night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:710
msgid "A mudlark who combs the Aldwater at low tide, shakes hard, and prices every rustle as a drowned wizard's spellbook. Her scroll cases are often full of river sand, which pours at the gentlest shake. Real parchment only rustles at a hard one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:712
msgid "Mud's been good to me!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:712
msgid "The river provides."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:713
msgid "Tide's turning. I'm off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:714
msgid "Back in the barrow, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:714
msgid "No skin off my nose."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:715
msgid "Ha! It's been through worse in the river."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:715
msgid "Oop!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:716
msgid "Oi! Mud or no mud, that's mine. It'll cost more now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:720
msgid "Sir Rowan Gale"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:720
msgid "Rowan"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:722
msgid "His grandfather's sword, and his family's hall back from the Guild, which foreclosed on it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:723
msgid "A Gale war chest. If my grandfather's sword's in it, it's mine, and I'll pay you {fee} for it. The rest is yours for {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:724
msgid "From the siege of Harrowgate. Any blade in it is my family's: {fee} for the best. {price} for the chest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:725
msgid "A knight without a war, whose family's hall the Guild foreclosed on. He's looking for his grandfather's sword. Prices by colour. If there are weapons in his chest, the best of them goes back to him for the price he names: value what's left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:727
msgid "Honour is satisfied."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:727
msgid "For the Gales!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:728
msgid "I'm expected at the lists. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:729
msgid "Then I shall keep looking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:729
msgid "Another chest, another day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:730
msgid "Have a care, sir!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:730
msgid "Steady!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:731
msgid "Have a care with my grandfather's things! It'll cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:739 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:739
msgid "Tick"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:742
msgid "Errands run, gold gone down the Gate, and one day off in three hundred years."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:743
msgid "Fresh through the Gate, from the Maw's own hoard. {price}. And the sand's already running, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:744
msgid "Errand for the Maw. A {colour} chest: {price}. Tick, tock."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:745
msgid "An imp courier with an hourglass, selling from the Maw's hoard. Prices by colour and never looks inside, and gives you twelve seconds to decide. Things from the Maw's hoard are often better than their chest's colour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:747
msgid "Delicious."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:747
msgid "A pleasure, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:748
msgid "Too slow! Back through the Gate I go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:749
msgid "Pfft. Your loss, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:749
msgid "Fine. Someone in the Emporium has more sense."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:750
msgid "Hee! Again!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:750
msgid "Clumsy mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:751
msgid "Careful, mortal! Breakages cost extra."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:755
msgid "Lord Sallow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:755
msgid "Sallow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:757
msgid "To win every bargain he makes. He always has."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:758
msgid "From the Maw's hoard. {price}, a pittance. My only condition: the dearest thing inside is mine."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:759
msgid "A bargain, mortal: {price}. When it opens, I take the best of it. Everything else is yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:760
msgid "A devil of the old law, who deals in bargains. His price is low, but the dearest thing inside is his. A chest of many middling things suits his deal; one grand thing and little else doesn't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:762
msgid "Signed and sealed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:762
msgid "A pleasure doing business. It always is."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:763
msgid "My time is worth more than yours, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:764
msgid "Another time. There is always another time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:764
msgid "How very wise of you. Or was it?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:765
msgid "Mind my bones."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:765
msgid "Tsk."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:766
msgid "Damaged goods cost more, mortal. Read the small print."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:770 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:770
msgid "Skrae"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:773
msgid "Out: away from the Gate, and the Maw, for good. It has heard enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:774
msgid "{price}, fairly. Then I clicked, like a bat, and listened. The echoes: {clue}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:775
msgid "I hear every coin in the realm, and every word the Maw says. {price}. My echoes: {clue}. Wards can't stop an echo."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:776
msgid "A demon with ears like a bat, who has heard enough of the Maw. It shakes a chest gently, then hard, and prices what it hears, fairly. Then it clicks and listens to the echoes, which come back off everything inside, warded or not: round is coin, long a weapon, soft a cloak, hollow a potion, flat a spell, tiny a gem. An echo you can't hear is warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:779
msgid "Fair."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:779
msgid "You won't regret it. Probably."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:780
msgid "I hear someone counting gold elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:781
msgid "I heard that coming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:781
msgid "Hm. Fair enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:782
msgid "Ow! My ears!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:782
msgid "Loud. Very loud."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:783
msgid "My ears! That will cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:787
msgid "Countess Vey"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:787
msgid "the Countess"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:790
msgid "To keep up appearances at court, a jewel at a time. Some of her gems are paste, and she knows which."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:791
msgid "From my strongroom. My gems, and whatever my maid packed. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:792
msgid "The gems alone are worth {price}, I'm told. The rest I couldn't say. My maid packs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:793
msgid "A countess of the court who knows her own jewels and nothing else: she prices her gems at what she paid for them, and whatever else her maid packed comes free. Some of her gems are paste, and she won't have a lodestone near them (half again if you try)."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:795
msgid "Charming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:795
msgid "Do look after them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:796
msgid "A lodestone? On MY gems? Half again, for the insult."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:797
msgid "I'm expected at court. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:798
msgid "How very disappointing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:798
msgid "Well. Someone at court will have it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:799
msgid "My gems!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:799
msgid "Must you?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:800
msgid "My gems! Half again, for the fright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:804
msgid "Madame Zell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:804
msgid "Zell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:807
msgid "To be right, and to be paid for it. The cards don't lie; Madame Zell doesn't either."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:808
msgid "A courtier's chest, sold for his gambling debts. Three from the Locking's deck: {clue}. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:809
msgid "The cards chose this one for you, dear. {clue}. A {colour} chest: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:810
msgid "The court's cartomancer. She draws three cards from the Locking's own deck for each chest: a suit drawn twice is what the ward holds (Coins, Swords for weapons, Mantles for cloaks, Cups for potions, Wands for spells, Stars for gems); three different suits, and nothing's warded. Prices by colour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:813
msgid "The cards are never wrong."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:813
msgid "As it was foretold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:814
msgid "The cards say I'm wanted elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:815
msgid "The cards did say you might."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:815
msgid "As you wish, dear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:816
msgid "I didn't see that coming. How rare."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:816
msgid "Oh!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:817
msgid "The cards warned me about you. Half again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:821 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:821
msgid "Gilt"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:824
msgid "The Maw's gilded iron sold as gold, so the Gate's gold buys more of the realm."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:825
msgid "Out of the Maw's hoard, friend, through a crack in the Gate. I'm leaving town tonight, so {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:826
msgid "Hoard goods, very rare. Gold and gems, every one of them. For you, just {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:827
msgid "The Maw's fence. He knows exactly what's in his chests, because he packed the demon gold himself: gilded iron sold as gold and gems, cheap. What's real comes cheap; the fakes are worth nothing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:829
msgid "Wonderful! No refunds."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:829
msgid "A pleasure. I really must be going."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:830
msgid "Can't stay. People to avoid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:831
msgid "Your loss, friend. Your very great loss."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:831
msgid "Suit yourself. I was never here."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:832
msgid "Easy, friend! Easy."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:832
msgid "Whoa there."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:833
msgid "Easy, friend! That'll cost a little extra."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:837
msgid "Old Aldo"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:837
msgid "Aldo"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:840
msgid "A Keywright he can trust with the one chest that matters."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:841
msgid "From an old house with a great many cellars. I've no idea what's in it. You tell me, and whatever you say it holds is my price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:842
msgid "Old things from an old house. Name what's inside: that's the price. Name it truly and I'll take a quarter off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:843
msgid "A tired old man in a plain cloak, with a very fine ring. He doesn't know what's in his chests: his price is whatever your slip says. Read it exactly and he takes a quarter off; read it wrong and you pay what it really holds, and a quarter more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:845
msgid "Well. We shall see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:845
msgid "Hm. Let's see what you heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:846
msgid "I'm needed elsewhere. Another day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:847
msgid "Another day, then. I'll be back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:847
msgid "Hm. A careful one. Good."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:848
msgid "Steady. It's older than both of us."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:848
msgid "Oh my."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:849
msgid "Steady! That was my grandfather's. I'll want a little more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:853
msgid "Avarax, the Gilded Maw"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:853
msgid "the Maw"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:856
msgid "Out."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:857
msgid "A trifle from my hoard. One coin. All I ask is that you open it here, where I can see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:858
msgid "One coin, little Keywright. And then everyone in this city will want twice as much today. Isn't that fun?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:859
msgid "The demon of greed himself, in a borrowed body dripping with rings. He sells a chest for one coin, but greed is catching: buy it, and everyone who comes to your counter after him that day asks twice as much."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:861
msgid "Yesss."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:861
msgid "Open it. Let me see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:862
msgid "I have all the time in the world. You don't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:863
msgid "Clever little thing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:863
msgid "Mm. Another day, then. There are so many days."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:864
msgid "Careful. I break things too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:864
msgid "Ha."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:865
msgid "Careful. Greed always wants more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:877
msgid "Sergeant Hollis"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:877
msgid "Hollis"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:878
msgid "Thieves caught and chests home; and to know why the Guild's foreclosed chests won't open for anyone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:879
msgid "The Wardens' sergeant at the Thornwick toll: posts the wanted notices, searches the market, pays a finder's share for a stolen chest sent home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:884
msgid "Nell Haddon"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:884
msgid "Nell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:885
msgid "Her father's note paid, his yard kept, and him home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:886
msgid "Old Haddon the wheelwright's daughter, who keeps his yard at the crossroads going with her own two hands."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:890
msgid "Old Haddon"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:890
msgid "Haddon"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:891
msgid "To make wheels, and never to sign anything again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:892
msgid "Brindle's wheelwright, who signed the Guild's paper for a new lathe."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:896
msgid "Tobias Fenn"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:896
msgid "Tobias"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:897
msgid "To know where the tithe goes, and not to vanish for asking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:898
msgid "A clerk in the Gilded Guild's counting-house, with ink to the elbows and doubts he shouldn't have."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:902
msgid "Mistress Aubel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:902
msgid "Aubel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:903
msgid "Every marked child in the county, for the Guild's counting-houses."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:904
msgid "A Guild Mark-Finder, who tests children's hands at every fair and takes the marked ones \"into the Guild's care\"."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:909
msgid "Sister Wren"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:909
msgid "Wren"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:910
msgid "To sing the Keyhold's song whole, once, before she dies."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:911
msgid "The last singer of the Keyhold's choir, blind since the night the Guild burned her chapel. She hums a song that stops halfway."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:915 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:915
msgid "Tock"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:916
msgid "To learn what's inside things, and then to be an apprentice."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:917
msgid "Archmage Orme's brass automaton, which opens chests with a Keywright's mark on a brass plate. It wears a cloak."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:921
msgid "Sir Edric Ashcombe"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:921
msgid "Sir Edric"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:922
msgid "To know that the Gate held, and then to keep his oath somewhere useful."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:923
msgid "A knight of King Aldric's guard, who locked himself into a chest at the Locking to guard the Crown's oath-book."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:928 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:928
msgid "Mabry"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:929
msgid "Drowned Fallowford's common chest home to its people, and her brother to write more often."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:930
msgid "Hesk's sister, from the river town the Guild drowned when it opened the Aldwater weir."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:934
msgid "Orrin Vash"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:934
msgid "Vash"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:935
msgid "To keep the best stall on Lantern Lane, which the Guild gave him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:936
msgid "A Guild-licensed trader of Crownhold, who sells from the Brightwaters' old stall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:940
msgid "Marta Brightwater"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:940
msgid "Marta"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:941
msgid "Her family's stall on Lantern Lane back, before she's too old to stand at it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:942
msgid "Rosa's mother, who kept the best stall on Lantern Lane for thirty years and taught Rosa to haggle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:946 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:946
msgid "Pemberton"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:947
msgid "House Marchmont whole again, or as near as he can manage."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:948
msgid "The Marchmonts' old steward, who stayed when the Guild took everything else, and keeps track of what it sold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:952
msgid "Wynn Hollow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:952
msgid "Wynn"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:953
msgid "Her son kept out of the Guild's counting-houses."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:954
msgid "Pip's mother, the mill's washerwoman."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:958
msgid "Harl Caskett"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:958
msgid "Caskett"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:959
msgid "The Old Wood's oak, felled and sold, on the Guild's account."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:960
msgid "The Gilded Guild's timber factor, with a deed for the Old Wood and a pen for whoever will witness it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:964
msgid "The Hawthorn Lady"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:964
msgid "the Hawthorn Lady"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:965
msgid "The Wood's oaks left standing; and a promise, kept."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:966
msgid "One of the fair folk of the Old Wood. She never used gold, and trades in promises."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:970
msgid "Lord Cassian Vell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:970
msgid "Cassian"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:972
msgid "Tonight's stake at cards. Tomorrow's, too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:973
msgid "Lady Isaura's brother, a gambler, selling his sister's chests cheap. They aren't his to sell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:974
msgid "Splendid. The tables await."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:974
msgid "Done. Not a word to my sister."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:975
msgid "Your loss. Someone will want it before the cards start."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:975
msgid "Pity."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:980
msgid "Jasper Wick"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:980
msgid "Jasper"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:981
msgid "A good ear, a low price, and no licence: and never to see the inside of a Guild counting-house."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:982
msgid "A hedge-wright: a Keywright without the Guild's licence, as Bram was for twenty years, trading from a cart."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:986
msgid "Sir Aldwin Gale"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:986
msgid "Sir Aldwin"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:987
msgid "His blade in his family's hands, and then to rest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:988
msgid "A knight who fell on Brindle Field the year before the Locking, and has walked it since."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:992
msgid "Martha Dunning"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:992
msgid "Martha"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:993
msgid "Thornwick's roads free and its market open, and the Old Wood left standing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:994
msgid "A Thornwick weaver, standing for reeve against the Guild's money with nothing but a loom and a loud voice."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:998
msgid "Sister Agathe"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:998
msgid "Agathe"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:999
msgid "Every chest left shut, as Saint Ide meant them; and to know who pays for the Unopened's bread."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1000
msgid "A preacher of the Unopened, the abbey's zealots, who say every chest opened feeds the Maw."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1004
msgid "Mother Tansy"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1004
msgid "Tansy"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1005
msgid "Her money back, with a third on top, on the morning she said."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1006
msgid "A moneylender of Lantern Lane, who lends to anyone short for the Guild and collects from everyone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1010
msgid "Mistress Ashby"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1010
msgid "Ashby"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1012
msgid "Her daughter's dowry, which the Corlews say is theirs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1013
msgid "A Thornwick widow whose daughter was to marry a Corlew, until the wedding wasn't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1014
msgid "There. The ward agrees with me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1015 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1024
msgid "Then the court will hear it again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1019
msgid "Hal Corlew"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1019
msgid "Corlew"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1021
msgid "His sister's dowry, which the Ashbys say is theirs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1022
msgid "A Thornwick carter whose sister was to marry into the Ashbys, until the wedding wasn't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1023
msgid "Knew it. Told them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1028
msgid "Jory Kettle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1028
msgid "Jory"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1029
msgid "To pay you back for his freedom, and to see the Guild's debt-houses emptied."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1030
msgid "Ada's son, two years in the Guild's debt-house for his father's tithe."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1064
msgid "a farmer at Brindle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1064
msgid "the Crossed Keys"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1064
msgid "the miller's wife"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1065
msgid "a carter on the forest road"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1065
msgid "a Thornwick family"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1065
msgid "the abbey's gatehouse"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1066
msgid "a Crownhold merchant"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1066
msgid "Lord Harrow's household"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1066
msgid "a family on Lantern Lane"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1066
msgid "a chapel by the Aldwater"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1067
msgid "a lady of the court"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1067
msgid "a palace steward"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1067
msgid "a banker of the Emporium"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1067
msgid "a courtier's widow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1081
msgid "Gods! It just... burst open! Keep the singing thing, then. The rest is going home with me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1085
msgid "one"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1085
msgid "two"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1085
msgid "three"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1085
msgid "four"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1085
msgid "five"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1085
msgid "six"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1086
msgid "seven"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1086
msgid "eight"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1090
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} and {1}"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Shop.cs:14
msgid "Bram's Stall"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Shop.cs:17 scripts/Core/Upgrades.cs:63
msgid "The Royal Emporium"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:45
msgid "The Hooded Woman"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:58 scripts/Ui/NotebookView.cs:328
msgid "Mara"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:59
msgid "King Aldric"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:63
msgid "The Magpie"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:88
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0}, for the Gilded Guild, about Bram's account. {1} in all this season: {2} payments, one every fifth night, and the first is {3}, {4} nights from now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:91 scripts/Core/Story.cs:107
msgid "And you, Keywright. We've met before, I think. You always look at my ring like that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:92
msgid "Every fifth night, as ever. A good ear pays any debt."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:98
#, csharp-format
msgid "Good evening. {0}, Collector for the Gilded Guild. I'm here about your uncle's account: twenty years open, and the Guild would like it settled this season."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:99
#, csharp-format
msgid "Good evening. {0}, Collector for the Gilded Guild. I'm here about Bram's account: twenty years open, and the Guild would like it settled this season."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:100
msgid "Twenty years. Has it been? Well. A debt's a debt."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:101
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} in all. {1} payments, one every fifth night, starting small: {2}, {3} nights from now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:102
msgid "Miss one, and the Guild takes the stall in settlement. A formality. I'm sure it won't come to that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:103
msgid "And each one paid, the Guild's carters move your stall a market further in: Thornwick, Crownhold, the Royal Emporium by the Gate. Richer chests pay richer dues."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:104
msgid "And the Guild is here to help, Keywright. We introduce customers, cart chests, lend where coin is short. Do ask."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:108
msgid "Every fifth night, then. A good ear pays any debt."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:124
#, csharp-format
msgid "Another year at the crossroads, {0}. The treasury's shut, the tea's hot, and the chests are waiting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:132
msgid "Darkness. Then two taps on the counter, and one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:133
msgid "I stayed away from the treasury. The dark came anyway, and then two taps on the counter, and one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:134
msgid "The last night came, and the dark with it. Then two taps on the counter, and one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:137
#, csharp-format
msgid "There you are, {0}. Another season at the crossroads. The Guild hasn't come sniffing yet."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:139
msgid "The first morning, again. I remember the treasury. I remember it breathing. He doesn't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:143
#, csharp-format
msgid "Another season at the crossroads, {0}. The Guild hasn't come sniffing yet. Let's make the most of it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:148
msgid "You know the trade, and the chests know you. Two taps and one when I want you at the counter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:151
msgid "Folk bring us chests nobody else can open. You buy one, it opens for you, and you sell what's inside. So listen before you buy: that's the whole trade."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:153
msgid "Bettany from the Crossed Keys will be by. She hears everything first, and she'll tell you most of it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:154
msgid "When I want you at the counter I'll tap it, twice and once. Like that. And mind: some chests listen back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:161 scripts/Core/Story.cs:172
msgid "A letter with the Guild's seal: \"Bram's handover is taking longer than expected. Keep the shop running until he returns.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:162
msgid "\"Earn the treasury key, keep his account paid, and bring the key to the treasury on the season's last night.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:163
msgid "The same letter, word for word. Last time, the treasury breathed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:169
msgid "A letter with the Guild's seal, and the terms it always sets: keep Bram's account paid every fifth night, earn the four pieces of the treasury key, and bring the key to the treasury on the season's last night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:173
msgid "\"Meanwhile the Guild's assessors will certify your work. Four marks of a master keywright earn the four pieces of the treasury key, each with a master's fee: a hidden thing read true, a stolen chest settled, a commission filled, an old lock picked without force.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:176
msgid "\"Pay Bram's account as it falls due, every fifth night, and bring the whole key to the treasury on the season's last night. His commission needs a second keywright. When it's done and his account is paid, he comes home.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:183
msgid "The tithe is paid. But the Gate is hungry, and the Guild has decided you owe it something for its patience."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:184
msgid "They'll keep coming, and every week they'll want half as much again. Let's see how long we can make them wait."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:193
msgid "Bram's welcome"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:194
msgid "The Guild's letter"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:195
msgid "Who stands with you"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:196
msgid "The Guild's terms"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:208
msgid "The last week of the tithe, and it's already paid: nobody's coming for anything this week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:209
msgid "The debt's last week. Pay it, and the Guild's carriage takes you and the key to the treasury."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:210
msgid "The debt's last week. Pay this, and Bram's account is closed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:212
msgid "Still no letter from Bram. The Guild's came on time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:224
msgid "A letter with the Guild's seal: \"The treasury opens on the season's last night. Bram looks forward to seeing you. Do bring the key.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:228
msgid "Vane was at the Crossed Keys last night, asking who your friends are."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:229
msgid "When you go to the treasury, who'll stand at the door with you, and take in whoever comes out?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:233
msgid "Nobody, it seems. Make some friends before the last night, or hire the bargemen at the Lantern Market."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:234
msgid "That's a crowd, that is. Whatever comes out of that treasury, it'll have somewhere to go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:235
msgid "It's a start. One more, before the last night, and they'll have somewhere to go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:250
msgid "One more thing. The Guild's treasury has asked for Bram. An old consignment needs his attention."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:251
msgid "Mind the stall. I'll write every week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:252
msgid "He won't write. I know where that carriage goes, and what waits at the end of the road."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:256
msgid "One more thing. The Guild's treasury has asked for Bram: an old consignment. The carriage is outside."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:257
#, csharp-format
msgid "Mind the stall, {0}. I'll write every week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:261
msgid "One more thing. The Guild's treasury has asked for Bram: an old consignment needs a keywright who knows it. Temporary work. The carriage is outside."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:262
msgid "The treasury? After twenty years they want me? Well. It's honest work, and it'll pay down the account."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:263
#, csharp-format
msgid "Mind the stall, {0}. I'll write every week. And keep my lamp lit: it's never let me down."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:264
msgid "Two taps and one, and I'll be back before you've missed me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:267
msgid "And Old Haddon comes with us. His note fell due tonight: he'll work it off at the treasury, with Bram."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:279
#, csharp-format
msgid "One more thing. The Guild has a note to collect tonight: {0}. They'll work it off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:284
msgid "Bram sends his regards. The handover's slow work, but he's in good spirits."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:285
msgid "The treasury opens on the season's last night. Bram is counting on you, and on the key."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:290
msgid "Bram is well, Keywright. Why go looking? Some doors are better left shut."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:292
msgid "You were at the toll, I hear. The palace road is no place for a shopkeeper."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:293
msgid "You remember more than you should, Keywright. So do I."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:299
msgid "Before you pay. The Guild could forget half of tonight's due, Keywright. All it asks is that your questions stop at the toll."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:300
msgid "Sensible. You'll find Sergeant Hollis has nothing to say to you this season."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:301
msgid "Then ask your questions. You'll find the answers heavy."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:305
#, csharp-format
msgid "Before you pay. You want Bram home. The Guild can have him at your door tomorrow, warm and whole. All it asks is your {0} piece of the key."
msgid_plural "Before you pay. You want Bram home. The Guild can have him at your door tomorrow, warm and whole. All it asks is your {0} pieces of the key."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:308
msgid "Done. He'll be home for breakfast. And you won't be at the treasury this season."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:309
msgid "Then he stays where he is. Gold keeps."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:318
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} week early"
msgid_plural "{0} weeks early"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:319
msgid "Before I've even come for it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:323
#, csharp-format
msgid "All of it? Now? {0}. Then Bram's account with the Guild is closed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:328
msgid "Free and clear, another year. Put the kettle on."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:332
msgid "Free and clear! Twenty years, and the account's closed. Look at my hand: it's warm."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:336
msgid "The treasury, then. Tonight. I'll send the carriage."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:337
msgid "And the treasury key is whole, I see. Then the Guild's carriage will take you to the treasury tonight. Bram is waiting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:339
#, csharp-format
msgid "The treasury opens on the season's last night. Bring the whole key: you're {0} piece short."
msgid_plural "The treasury opens on the season's last night. Bring the whole key: you're {0} pieces short."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:343
msgid "No key? Then the Guild will open the treasury without you tonight. Bram will be so disappointed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:352
msgid "Cold. I'm so cold. And this is our stall. Two taps and one: I heard you knock back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:354
msgid "Twenty years ago the Mark-Finders came for you: a marked baby, at the crossroads. I pledged them my hand, mark and all. That was my account."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:355
msgid "Twenty years ago the Mark-Finders came for a marked baby, my niece Kit. I pledged them my hand, mark and all. That was my account."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:356
msgid "This spring they called it in. The treasury was never a job. It was a scale, and a crate, and the dark."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:357
msgid "And now look: you paid it. Put the kettle on. Tonight we're just two people in a shop."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:360
msgid "I've brought him home before. He doesn't remember it. I don't want to do it again: I want it to last."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:370
msgid "The key, whole. The register. A full mimic, asleep in a basket. And friends at the door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:372
msgid "Whatever's in there, we take them home. All of them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:373
msgid "Keywright. You've brought company. No matter: the chest is waiting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:378
msgid "The carriage, Keywright. You know the way."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:381
msgid "The carriage, Keywright. The treasury is under the palace, and Bram's commission is waiting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:382
msgid "Here it is: the old consignment. The treasury's great chest. The Guild has never been able to open it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:383
msgid "You have the key. Open it, and Bram's account is closed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:389
msgid "You have already saved him once. I can make this time remain. Take him home. Leave the door to me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:390
msgid "I can make this time remain. Take them home. Leave the door to me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:393
msgid "He knows whom he came to save. But you still want to see what is inside."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:398
msgid "The next morning came. Bram brought the tea, and the market opened, and every chest on every stall wore the Guild's seal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:399
msgid "By noon there was nothing anyone could buy that the treasury hadn't sold them. By evening it wanted the road, and the river, and the light."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:400
msgid "It can't keep a bargain. It can't stop wanting. It reached past the door for everything, and the seal woke."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:406
msgid "Morning. Tea's hot. Here: feel my hand. Warm as the pot."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:409
msgid "Day twenty-one. I've never seen the calendar say that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:410
msgid "The morning after the treasury, and nothing's turned back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:411
msgid "Old Haddon's in his yard, swearing at a lathe. Half the crossroads walked home last night, and nobody can say from where."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:412
msgid "Keywright! The waterwheel's broken, and my father's old millwright's chest has the only tools that fit it. Open it for us?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:418
msgid "That's them! The wheel will turn by noon. Bless you, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:419
msgid "Treasure's still treasure. But that's the best thing we've opened all year, and I'll fight anyone who says different."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:420
msgid "Two taps on the counter, and one. The next customer. The shop goes on."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:427
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} weeks, and every coin of the tithe paid. Let them have the building: they can't have the mark."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:428
msgid "So soon? Well. We'll start again somewhere. A good ear is never broke for long."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:429
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} weeks. You did better than I ever did. We'll start again somewhere."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:431
msgid "The last night will come without me, and the treasury will open with Bram in it. And then it'll be spring."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:446
msgid "The Wardens have the palace road. No Guild carriage gets past my toll tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:447
msgid "The Wardens will hold the palace road, when it comes to it. You've sent enough chests home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:449
msgid "Half of Brindle walked to the palace to see it opened. The Guild's men can't get through the crowd."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:450
msgid "Brindle's with you: half the crossroads would walk to the palace if you asked them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:452
msgid "A black feather on the counter: the Guild's carriages have lost their wheels in Lantern Lane. All of them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:453
msgid "A black feather on the counter, and a note: \"When the Guild comes for you, the Lockless will be in its way.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:455
msgid "The palace guard is at the treasury door. My Guild has no business here tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:456
msgid "The Crown's with you, Keywright. I've a palace guard with very little to do."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:458
msgid "Hawthorn has grown across the Guild's road. They'll be all night cutting through it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:459
msgid "The Wood keeps its own. When they come for you, they'll find thorns."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:461
msgid "Ironroot's smiths have barred the Gate road with iron. Let the Guild try lifting it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:462
msgid "Ironroot owes you a crown. Ask, and you'll have a hundred dwarves at your door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:467
msgid "I'll hold the lamp, master! I'm not scared. Much."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:467
msgid "I'll stand with you, master. I'm small, but I'm quick."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:469
msgid "Father brought his cart. Whoever comes out of there rides home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:469
msgid "Father says he owes you a cart, and a wheel, and his neck. Call us."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:476
msgid "The whole mill's here, and every one of us has a washing paddle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:476
msgid "Send for me, and the whole mill comes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:477
msgid "Rafe's sword's at the door, dear, and Jory's holding it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:477
msgid "Rafe would have stood with you. So will we, dear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:478
msgid "I've brought two delvers and a lot of rope. Nobody's getting through that door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:478
msgid "You dug me out of the Barrow. I'll dig you out of anything."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:479
msgid "The Crossed Keys is closed tonight. Everyone's here instead."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:479
msgid "The Crossed Keys stands with you, love. Every last drunk in it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:480
msgid "A Gale at the door, with a Gale's blade. Let them come."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:480
msgid "The Gales pay their debts. Call, and I'll be there."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:481
msgid "Goblins in the Guild's cellar. Lots of goblins. Very busy."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:481
msgid "The clan comes when you call. All of it. Even the uncles."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:482
msgid "House Vell is at the palace, and so, for once, is my brother."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:482
msgid "House Vell owes you. We pay our debts, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:483
msgid "Ironroot's here, Keywright, with hammers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:483
msgid "A hundred dwarves, when you need them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:484
msgid "A hedge-wright at your back. Two Keywrights are harder to stop than one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:484
msgid "When the Guild comes, send for the hedge-wright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:485
msgid "I've brought the Roll. Whatever the Guild says tonight, the charter says otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:485
msgid "The Roll will say what the Crown pledged, when it matters."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:486
msgid "Every lamp in the Arcanum is lit tonight. The Guild won't find a shadow to hide in."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:486
msgid "The Arcanum's apprentices will stand with you. Some of the archmages, too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:487
msgid "Two whole families are here, dear: the ones you married off. They'd like a word with the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:487
msgid "Two families owe you their wedding, dear. They'll come."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:488
msgid "Brought the plough horses. The Guild's carriages can go round."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:488
msgid "Call, and the whole fair comes, horses and all."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:489
msgid "I carried chests for you. Tonight I'll carry anything that tries to get past this door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:489
msgid "I owe you my freedom. Call, and I'll come."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:490
msgid "The Wet Hen's at the river stairs, if anyone needs to leave in a hurry."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:490
msgid "Need anything carried away from the Guild quietly? Ask for the Wet Hen."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:506
msgid "No Heartsong this season. Don't take it hard: most seasons never hear one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:507
msgid "They're the rarest things in Aldmark. Nine of them, things loved more than gold, sung into the Locking and lost among millions of chests. About one season in three turns one up."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:509
msgid "Only a Keywright hears one. At the gentlest shake it sings a tune no other thing makes, and the seller never knows it's there: they price the chest as if it weren't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:511
msgid "Nobody would pay a penny for one. But on display, each does one great thing for the shop that no gold can buy, for as long as it sings: the kind of thing a whole season can be built around."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:513
msgid "So shake every chest gently first, and listen. The collection's Heartsongs page keeps a place for each of the nine."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:523
msgid "So you're Hesk. A partner with the mark and an honest scale: I'll take it. Mind the stall, mind your back, and half of it's yours when the Guild's paid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:525
msgid "Rosa Brightwater, as I live. Your mother sold me my first lock-pick, forty years back. My mark's faded: mind the stall, partner, and half of it's yours when the Guild's paid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:527
msgid "Lady Marchmont. Your grandfather and I opened chests together, before your house was grand. My mark's faded: mind my stall, and put your collection on the shelf. The Guild's paid out of the takings."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:529
#, csharp-format
msgid "There you are, {0}! Look at your hand: the mark's yours now. And so is the stall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:542
msgid "So. Let me tell you what became of everyone, this season."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:543
msgid "Pull up a stool, love. Here's what became of everyone this season."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:550
msgid "And you, Hesk. A grocer from a drowned town, with the mark on your hand. What becomes of you is up to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:551
msgid "And you, Rosa. A Brightwater of Lantern Lane, with the mark on your hand. What becomes of you is up to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:552
msgid "And you, my lady. The last Marchmont, with the mark on your hand. What becomes of you is up to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:553
msgid "And you, Kit. My kin, with the mark on your hand. What becomes of you is up to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:554
msgid "And you. Bram's kin, with the mark on your hand. What becomes of you is up to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:567
msgid "The treasury's shut for good, and everyone who came out of it is home. Nobody can say from where, and nobody asks."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:570
msgid "And I'm home. You brought me out of that chest with all the rest, and I still can't say it without shaking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:571
msgid "And I'm home. You had me out of my Guild crate before that night, and I still can't say it without shaking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:575
msgid "I came home on the Guild's word, warm and whole. I don't know what you gave them for it, and I jump at every tap on the counter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:576
msgid "I'm home, and my hand is warm. You brought me out of a Guild crate, and I still can't say it without shaking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:578
msgid "Bram's account is closed, every coin paid, and Bram never came home. The Guild says the treasury keeps long hours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:580
msgid "The Guild took the stall, and Bram never came home. Nobody's had a letter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:582
msgid "Old Haddon walked home from a Guild crate, cold as a well. He's making wheels again, and he won't sign anything."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:584
msgid "Old Haddon kept his yard, because somebody paid his note. He's making you a wheel. You don't need one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:586
msgid "Old Haddon never came home from working off his note. Nell keeps the yard, and a lamp in the window."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:589
#, csharp-format
msgid "And you sold {0} gold thing to the Maw's buyers. Every coin of it an eye for him. I hope it was worth it."
msgid_plural "And you sold {0} gold things to the Maw's buyers. Every coin of it an eye for him. I hope it was worth it."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:592
msgid "And there's still a mimic in the back room, asleep on the gold. Don't wake it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Story.cs:594
msgid "And on the last night the Guild opened the treasury without me. I know what comes after: two taps, and one, and spring."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:62
#, csharp-format
msgid ", {0} or better"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:81
msgid "Goldsmith"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:81
msgid "Coin and gems"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:82
#, csharp-format
msgid "Moneychangers and jewellers come your way: coin and gems turn up {0} more often, and they sell for {1} more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:86
msgid "Armourer"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:87
#, csharp-format
msgid "Soldiers, knights and dwarves come {0} more often, and weapons sell for {1} more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:91
msgid "Apothecary"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:92
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0}, and potions sell for {1} more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:92
msgid "Glass never breaks, dropped or forced"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:92
#, csharp-format
msgid "Glass is {0} less likely to break"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:96
msgid "Spellkeeper"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:97
#, csharp-format
msgid "People trust you with secrets: chests are {0} likelier to have a false bottom, and spells sell for {1} more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:101
msgid "Cloakmaker"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:102
#, csharp-format
msgid "Fine drapery: your exhibition counts +{0}, and cloaks sell for {1} more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:106
msgid "Keen Eye"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:106
msgid "Perfect reads in a row"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:106
msgid "perfect reads in a row"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:108
#, csharp-format
msgid "A perfect read earns you a valuer's fee: {0} of what the chest held."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:112
msgid "Lucky Shop"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:112
msgid "Surprises"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:112
msgid "things better than their chest"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:114
#, csharp-format
msgid "Luck follows a lucky shop: everything you open is {0} likelier to come out a step better."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:118
msgid "Finder"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:118
msgid "False bottoms and wards"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:118
msgid "hidden or warded things found"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:120
#, csharp-format
msgid "Chests are {0} likelier to have a false bottom, and what you find under one or name in a ward sells for {1} more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:124
msgid "Haggler"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:124
msgid "Chests talked down"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:124
msgid "chests talked down or named a price for"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:126
#, csharp-format
msgid "Word of a hard bargainer: hagglers and sellers who wait for an offer settle for {0} less."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:130
msgid "Arcanist"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:130
msgid "Enchanted things found"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:130
msgid "enchanted things"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Synergies.cs:132
#, csharp-format
msgid "Mages seek you out: each thing is {0} likelier to be enchanted, and enchanted things sell for {1} more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:19
msgid "The Hedge-wright"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:20
msgid "Jasper Wick has the Key-mark and no Guild licence, as Bram once had, and he's parked his cart across the road from your stall. He takes a customer a day off you, and the Guild's Mark-Finder is asking after hedge-wrights."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:29
msgid "Jasper Wick, hedge-wright, at your service and everyone else's. That's my cart across the road. No licence, no tithe, no Guild: just a good ear and a low price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:31
msgid "There's room at the Crossroads for two of us, isn't there? I'll take the folk you're too slow for."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:35
msgid "Jasper Wick, a hedge-wright, set up his cart across the road. He takes one of your customers a day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:42
msgid "Mistress Aubel, for the Gilded Guild. A hedge-wright is trading at this crossroads without the Guild's licence. You'll have seen him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:44
#, csharp-format
msgid "The Guild takes hedge-wrights into its counting-houses, as it takes marked children. A name is worth {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:47
msgid "Jasper Wick, across the road"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:55
msgid "You gave the Mark-Finder Jasper Wick's name. The Guild took him, cart and all."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:56
msgid "The Guild thanks you, Keywright. A licensed trade is a safe trade."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:59
msgid "I've seen no hedge-wright"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:62
msgid "You told the Mark-Finder you'd seen no hedge-wright. Bram was one for twenty years."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:63
msgid "No? Then he's a quick one. The Guild will find him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:71
msgid "Let's settle it like Keywrights: one chest, read in front of the Crossed Keys. Read it right and I'll take my cart to Thornwick. Wrong, and I stay. One coin, and it's yours either way."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:82
msgid "You read Jasper's chest exactly right in front of the whole Crossed Keys. He took his cart to Thornwick, and his customers came to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:88
msgid "You read Jasper's chest wrong in front of the whole Crossed Keys. His cart stays across the road."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:94
msgid "You wouldn't read against Jasper. His cart stays across the road."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:100
msgid "Jasper at the back door, his cart packed. \"You've a better ear than me, and you kept the Guild off me besides. If you ever need a hedge-wright's help, send to the Lockless in Thornwick. They'll find me.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:105
msgid "Jasper Wick owes you a favour: you kept the Guild off him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:114
msgid "The Field's Dead"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:115
msgid "Garrick's plough turned up a knight's chest on Brindle Field, where the last battle was fought. The blade inside has a name on it, and that night the knight's ghost comes knocking: he wants it home, to his blood."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:127
msgid "My plough turned this up on the Field, deep, under a knight's shield. Finder's right: it's mine to sell, and I'd sooner not keep it in the house. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:134
msgid "You bought the knight's chest Garrick ploughed up. Bram set the knight's blade aside: it has a name on it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:136
msgid "You passed on the knight's chest Garrick ploughed up."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:142
msgid "A cold knock, and an old knight in rusted mail at the back door, with the moon through him. \"That blade is mine. Aldwin Gale. I fell on that field before the Locking.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:144
msgid "\"Give it to my blood. There were Gales in Crownhold, once. I have waited three hundred years: I can wait a little more.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:147
msgid "I'll find your family"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:150
msgid "Sir Aldwin Gale's ghost asked you to send his blade to his blood, the Gales of Crownhold. You promised."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:151
msgid "\"Then I can rest a while.\" And he's gone, and the night's warm again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:153
#, csharp-format
msgid "Finder's right: it's mine to sell ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:158
msgid "You sold Sir Aldwin's blade. His ghost walks the Crossroads at dusk now, and folk stay home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:159
msgid "\"Then I'll walk.\" The lamps gutter. Out on the Field, something starts to march."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:167
msgid "Bram says you've a blade for me? \"Aldwin Gale\" on the tang... my great-great-grandfather's. The Guild sold our hall, but it never had this. Where did you find it?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:169
msgid "I can't pay what it's worth. But my house has a claim on the best blade in any chest I sell, and from today it's yours, not mine. And the Gales owe you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:177
msgid "You gave Sir Rowan his ancestor's blade. The best weapon in his chests is yours now, and the Gales owe you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:183
msgid "One last cold knock. \"My blood has my blade. I can lie down now. Take this: it was in my purse when I fell, and I've no use for it.\" A coin, three hundred years old, warm as a hand."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:189
msgid "Sir Aldwin Gale lay down at last, and left you his lucky coin."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:198
msgid "The Crossed Keys"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:199
msgid "The Guild has doubled the Crossed Keys' tithe, and Bettany Crane is a purse short. If she can't pay, the Guild seals the inn, and the crossroads loses its taproom and its news."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:208
msgid "The Guild's doubled the inn's tithe, love. \"The Crossed Keys does a good trade\", Vane says. It did, till he came."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:209
#, csharp-format
msgid "I'm {0} short, and they'll seal the doors if I can't pay. Lend it me, and you'll have it back and half again by the next Guild night. On my mother's grave."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:213
#, csharp-format
msgid "Lend her the money ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:218
msgid "Bettany, to repay you"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:219
msgid "You lent Bettany what she was short for the Guild. She'll pay you back, and half again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:220
msgid "You're a love. Half again, by the next Guild night. On my mother's grave."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:222
msgid "I can't spare it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:225
msgid "You couldn't lend Bettany what she was short for the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:226
msgid "No. No, of course. Who has, these days?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:234
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0}, love: what I owed and half again. The Crossed Keys is still mine. If you ever need a room, a meal or a word in the right ear, it's yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:242
msgid "Bettany paid you back, and half again. The Crossed Keys stays open, and she owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:248
msgid "A Guild notice, nailed to the Crossed Keys' door and copied to every shop at the crossroads: \"SEALED for tithe unpaid, by order of the Gilded Guild. Marrow, Bailiff.\" Bettany's gone north to her sister's."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:254
msgid "The Guild sealed the Crossed Keys for its tithe. Bettany has gone north, and won't be back this season."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:263
msgid "The Harvest Fair"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:264
msgid "The harvest fair comes to Brindle, with a chest to be read in front of the whole county. Garrick wants the new Keywright to put up the prize, and then to read it exactly."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:274
msgid "Harvest fair's the day after tomorrow, and the whole county comes. There's a reading contest: a chest nobody's opened, and a prize for whoever reads it right."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:276
#, csharp-format
msgid "Bram always put up the prize. Will you? {0}, and your name on the banner."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:279
#, csharp-format
msgid "Put up the prize ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:283
msgid "You put up the harvest fair's prize. Your name's on the banner, and the county will come past the stall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:284
msgid "Bram's stall, on the banner! Half the county'll come past it on the day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:286
msgid "Not this year"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:288
msgid "You didn't put up the harvest fair's prize. The miller did."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:289
msgid "The miller, then. He'll want his name bigger than Bram's ever was."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:298
msgid "The fair's chest! Read it right in front of the whole county, and the prize is yours: your own money back, and the miller's on top. One coin to enter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:300
msgid "The fair's chest, and the miller's prize. Read it right in front of the whole county and it's yours. One coin to enter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:309
msgid "You read the fair's chest exactly right, and won the prize. The county cheered; Garrick says he owes you a pint and a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:314
msgid "You read the fair's chest wrong, in front of the whole county. The miller's boy won."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:317
msgid "You didn't enter the fair's reading contest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:326
msgid "The Guild took Jasper Wick to a counting-house, and sold his cart. He was a hedge-wright, like I was. I keep thinking that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:328
msgid "I've a cellar in Crownhold now, and the Lockless bring me every chest their grandmothers ever locked. Best ear at the Crossroads? Yours, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:330
msgid "Still across the road, still cheaper than you, and still no licence. Come and have a drink with the competition some time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:331
msgid "Jasper Wick traded across the road all season. The Guild never caught him. I hope it never does."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:337
msgid "Great-great-grandfather's blade hangs in the Gales' hall again, and he walks no more. The Gales don't forget a debt, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:339
msgid "Sir Aldwin still walks Brindle Field at dusk, looking for his blade. Garrick won't plough the north end. Can't blame him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:341
msgid "Sir Aldwin's blade is still in our back room, waiting for a Gale. He's patient. He's had the practice."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:342
msgid "Sold the knight's chest to a tinker in the end. He came back the next week, white as milk, and gave it back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:356
msgid "The Crossed Keys is still mine, love, and there's always a pint behind the bar with your name on it. Bram's too, the old soak."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:358
msgid "The Guild sealed the Crossed Keys. Bettany's up north with her sister. The crossroads is quieter than I've ever known it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:359
msgid "I found the money in the end. Don't ask where, love."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:366
msgid "Put up the prize and won it back! Folk are still talking about it. Best harvest fair since Bram's day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:367
msgid "The miller's still sore you won his prize. Best harvest fair since Bram's day, and that's saying something."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:369
msgid "The miller's boy read the fair's chest better than Bram's Keywright. He'll never let you forget it, and neither will I."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Brindle.cs:370
msgid "Your name was on the banner, and the county came. Next year, enter the contest too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:35
msgid "Bram's Account"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:36
msgid "Bram's twenty-year account with the Gilded Guild falls due this season. Keep it paid, and mind what the Guild wants with him: the notebook's Inquiry page keeps what you learn, and how the treasury key is coming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:45
msgid "My granddad's old green chest, from the attic. I've meant to sell it for years. {price}, and it's yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:55
msgid "The Guild's men were at the yard. Father signed their paper for a new lathe, and it falls due on their first night: forty gold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:56
msgid "If it isn't paid they'll take the yard, and him with it, to work it off. He says it's only work. I don't like how they said it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:59
msgid "I've seen this before: the Guild's carriage took him with Bram, and he never came home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:61
msgid "I've paid it before. He made me a wheel I didn't need, and he was home all season."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:66
#, csharp-format
msgid "Pay his note ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:72
msgid "You paid Old Haddon's note to the Guild before its first night. He's staying home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:73
msgid "You'd do that? He'll pay you back in wheels. Whether you want them or not."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:75
msgid "I can't, not this week"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:77
msgid "Nell Haddon told you the Guild has her father's note, due on its first night. You couldn't help."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:78
msgid "No. Nobody can. I'll find it somewhere."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:91
msgid "A lot of the Guild's repossessed goods: tools, mostly, and a tuning fork with a tag on it. Nobody's claimed them. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:97
msgid "In a lot of the Guild's repossessed goods: Bram's tuning fork, tagged from the weighhouse on the palace road. Not the treasury."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:106
msgid "Sergeant Hollis, off duty. \"You've that look again, like you know what I'm going to say. The Guild's carts? Every fifth night, down the palace road. Come to the toll, if you mean it.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:109
msgid "Sergeant Hollis, off duty and uneasy. \"Guild carts pass my toll every fifth night, under sacking. They don't stop at the Guild Hall: they go on down the palace road.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:111
msgid "\"Last week a sack slipped. It was a man, Keywright. A gold man. Next Guild night, I'm following one. Come with me, if you've the stomach.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:114
msgid "Meet him at the toll on the Guild's night"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:117
msgid "Bring a dark coat. And don't rattle anything."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:119
msgid "Not this season"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:119
msgid "Suit yourself. The carts'll keep coming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:129
msgid "Fell off a Guild cart on the palace road. Heavy as sin, Guild seal and all, and nobody's asking after it. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:130
msgid "You bought a Guild crate that fell off a cart on the palace road."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:131
msgid "Corvin had a Guild crate off the palace road. You let it go on to the treasury."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:141
msgid "The Wardens stopped a Guild cart at my toll. This crate's chalked with a name you'd know. It's yours, Keywright. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:150
msgid "A Guild crate off the palace road, chalked with a name. The bargemen say you were asking. {price}, and I never saw it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:160
msgid "From the crypt. It's warm, Keywright. Warm like bread. The brothers want it gone. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:168
msgid "A woman in a grey hood, who looks at you a long time. \"You remember a spring that hasn't happened yet. I can see it on you.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:169
msgid "\"I'm Mara, the last of the Keyhold. We gave the seal a last clause: if the Maw ever breaks out without leave, the year turns back to its first morning.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:171
msgid "\"Whoever has touched the seal's core remembers. So does he. Nobody else.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:172
msgid "\"The Guild doesn't own that chest, Keywright. Find out what the Crown actually pledged. Master Quire keeps the Roll.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:177
msgid "Mara of the Keyhold told you the seal's last clause: when the Maw breaks out without leave, the year turns back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:185
msgid "Master Quire, the Archivist, with the Roll open on your counter. \"The treasury. Here: pledged by the Crown to the Gilded Guild, ten years since. Its keys, and its takings.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:187
msgid "\"Not its people. Not a keywright's word. The Crown never owned those to pledge. The Guild can let you in. It can't make you give.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:191
msgid "Master Quire showed you the treasury's charter: the Crown pledged its keys and takings to the Guild, not its people, nor a keywright's word."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:198
msgid "Ten years ago there was a famine, and the Crown had nothing it could spend. So I pledged my treasury to the Guild: its keys, and its takings."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:199
msgid "Not my people, Keywright. Not your word. A king can't pledge what was never his."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:203
msgid "Old Aldo told you what the Crown pledged to the Guild: the treasury's keys and takings, not its people, nor your word."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:211
msgid "\"The Guild registers its crates in the Roll like any chest. I could copy the weighhouse pages for you. The ink's dear.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:214
#, csharp-format
msgid "Have him copy them ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:217
msgid "Every crate, by name and weight, and the night it goes down. Burn it after."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:219
msgid "The Roll keeps."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:228
msgid "A note under the door, in Mara's hand: \"You asked what the Maw is. Before there were Locking chests there was one chest. It was empty, and it wanted.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:229
msgid "\"We didn't invent the Locking, Keywright. We copied it, and shut it in its own chest. It can't have enough. That's all it is.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:237
msgid "The cart went down the palace road to a long, low hall that smelled of hot metal. Hollis called it the weighhouse."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:238
msgid "Crates in rows, each chalked with a name and a weight. \"H. Haddon, 14 stone.\" \"Bram, keywright, 13 stone.\" A clerk read them off a register."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:239
msgid "\"People,\" Hollis whispered. \"They're weighing people, Keywright.\" You copied the register's page before the lamps went out."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:245
msgid "You followed a Guild cart with Sergeant Hollis to the weighhouse: crates, each with a name and a weight. Bram's among them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Campaign.cs:256
msgid "Bram is home: freed from a Guild crate, his pledge redeemed. He told you what he pledged, twenty years ago."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:19
msgid "Tilly Mudge the mudlark hears a bell ringing under the Aldwater at night, and nobody believes her. If she's right, something has been chained to it since the Locking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:28
msgid "There's a bell under the Aldwater. I hear it nights, off the old stairs below the palace, ringing when there's no wind and no current. Nobody believes me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:30
msgid "A mudlark hears what's in the mud. Same as you hear what's in a chest. You believe me, don't you?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:33
msgid "I believe you"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:36
msgid "Tilly Mudge hears a bell under the Aldwater. You believe her."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:37
msgid "You do? Then I'll find exactly where. Give me two days."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:39
msgid "The river's full of noises"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:41
msgid "Tilly Mudge hears a bell under the Aldwater. You didn't believe her."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:42
msgid "It is. And one of them's a bell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:50
msgid "Found it. Under the Keyhold stairs, where the archmages used to come down to the water. It's big, and there's something chained to it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:52
#, csharp-format
msgid "A barge and a dredge for a day is {0}. Finder's right: whatever comes up, half's yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:55
#, csharp-format
msgid "Hire the barge ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:58
msgid "Tilly, with the bell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:59
msgid "You hired a barge to dredge Tilly's bell out of the Aldwater."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:60
msgid "Two days, and we'll have it up. Bring a towel."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:62
msgid "Too dear"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:64
msgid "You wouldn't pay to dredge Tilly's bell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:65
msgid "Then it'll ring down there a while longer."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:76
msgid "Up it came, a bell as big as a cart, and this chained to the clapper. Finder's right: half each, and this half's yours. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:82
msgid "Tilly's bell came up out of the Aldwater, with a chest chained to its clapper: your half, freely given."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:87
msgid "Tilly's bell came up out of the Aldwater. You let her keep the chest that was chained to it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:94
msgid "The hooded woman at the back door, soaked to the knees. \"That's the Keyhold's bell. We rang it from the river stairs, and when the Locking was made we hid something in its clapper.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:96
msgid "\"It's empty. Someone was there before us, long ago. Take this for the trouble: Keyhold silver, from the bell's crown.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:100
msgid "The Keyhold's bell was empty. The Hooded Woman paid you in Keyhold silver for the trouble."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:109
msgid "The Moneylender"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:110
msgid "Mother Tansy of Lantern Lane lends to anyone short for the Guild, against next week's first morning, a third on top. Pay her back and she lends again on better terms; don't, and her men come for your shelf."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:119
msgid "Mother Tansy, of Lantern Lane. Short for the Guild? Everyone in Crownhold is, dear. That's my living."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:120
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} now, and {1} on the first morning of next week. If it's not there, I take something nice off your shelf. Fair's fair."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:124 scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:145
#, csharp-format
msgid "Borrow it (+{0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:127
msgid "You borrowed from Mother Tansy, to pay back with a third on top on the first morning of next week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:128
msgid "Lovely. My man will call. He's very punctual."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:130
msgid "No, thank you"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:132
msgid "You wouldn't borrow from Mother Tansy."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:133
msgid "You know where I am, dear. Everyone does, sooner or later."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:141
msgid "You paid on the nail, dear. I like that in a Keywright. So: better terms."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:142
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} now, and only a quarter on top, on the first morning of next week. For a grander shop, perhaps?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:148
msgid "You borrowed from Mother Tansy again, on better terms: a quarter on top."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:149
msgid "Lovely. Same as before, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:151
msgid "I'm square, and I'll stay square"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:153
msgid "You didn't borrow from Mother Tansy again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:154
msgid "Sensible. Dull, but sensible."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:164
msgid "The Duel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:165
msgid "Sir Rowan Gale and Lord Cassian Vell will fight on the Aldwater steps at dawn, and someone honest has to hold both their stakes overnight. Lord Cassian has never been honest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:174
msgid "Lord Cassian Vell called the Gales a family of debtors across a card table. We meet on the Aldwater steps at dawn, the day after tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:176
msgid "We each stake a chest, and the winner takes both. Someone honest must hold them. A Keywright's back room, I thought."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:179
msgid "I'll hold the stakes"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:183
msgid "You're holding the stakes for Sir Rowan's duel with Lord Cassian, in your back room."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:184
msgid "Thank you. Dawn, the day after tomorrow. Come and watch, if you've the stomach."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:186
msgid "It's not my quarrel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:188
msgid "You wouldn't hold the stakes for Sir Rowan's duel."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:189
msgid "No. I suppose it isn't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:197
msgid "Lord Cassian at the back door, smelling of brandy, with a purse. \"Hand me both stakes tonight, and this is yours. Rowan need never know where they went.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:201
#, csharp-format
msgid "Take his purse ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:208
msgid "You sold the duel's stakes to Lord Cassian. Sir Rowan left Crownhold in disgrace, and won't trade with you again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:209
msgid "\"Splendid. Not a word to anyone, Keywright. Least of all my sister.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:211
msgid "The stakes stay where they are"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:214
msgid "Lord Cassian tried to buy the duel's stakes off you. You sent him away."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:215
msgid "\"Honest. How very tiresome.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:224
msgid "I fought with great-great-grandfather's blade, and Cassian's sword broke on it at the third pass. The stakes are mine. A tenth is yours for holding them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:226
msgid "Cassian slipped on the wet steps at the third pass, and yielded. The stakes are mine. A tenth is yours for holding them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:227
msgid "Cassian fights better drunk than I do sober. He has the stakes, and I've a cut to remember him by. He left a tenth for you, for holding them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:236
msgid "Sir Rowan won his duel with Lord Cassian. You were paid for holding the stakes, and the Gales owe you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:237
msgid "Lord Cassian won his duel with Sir Rowan. You were paid for holding the stakes, and Rowan owes you a favour for your honesty."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:246
msgid "The Archive Fire"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:247
msgid "Someone has set the Royal Archive alight, and the Chest Roll with it: the record of who owns every chest in Aldmark. It's burning tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:256
msgid "A boy hammering at the back door: \"The Archive's burning! Master Quire's carrying the Roll out himself, and he can't lift the half of it!\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:258
msgid "You can see the glow over the rooftops from here. It'll take all night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:261
msgid "Run to help"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:266
msgid "You ran to the Archive fire and carried the Chest Roll out with Master Quire, all night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:267
msgid "You're out of the door before the boy's finished. Nim will find the back door shut tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:269
msgid "It's not my fire"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:274
msgid "Half the Chest Roll burned in the Archive fire. Master Quire is ruined, and won't be trading this season."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:275
msgid "The glow lasts till dawn. In the morning, half of Crownhold smells of burnt parchment."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:283
msgid "We saved the Roll. Every volume. And the fire started in a lamp-oil cask with the Guild's own stamp on it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:284
msgid "The Guild wanted the Archive's ledgers of its seizures burnt. Here: a fair copy, in your hand and mine. Keep it somewhere they won't think to look."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:290
msgid "Master Quire gave you a copy of the Archive's ledgers of the Guild's seizures. A paper for the case against the Guild. He owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:317
msgid "The Keyhold's bell hangs over the river stairs again, and I ring it for the ferry. The hooded lady paid in Keyhold silver. A mudlark heard it first!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:319
msgid "The bell came up, and I ring it for the ferry now. The posh ones call me the bell-finder. I call me rich."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:320
msgid "It still rings down there, nights. You believed me, though. That's something."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:326
msgid "You owed me, dear, and I took what you owed off your shelf. No hard feelings. Business is business."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:328
msgid "Paid on the nail, every time. If you ever want to go into lending, dear, I'd take you as a partner."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:329
msgid "You never borrowed a penny from me. I don't know whether to admire you or worry about you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:335
msgid "Sir Rowan left Crownhold after the duel that never was. Cassian tells everyone he won it. You know better."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:337
msgid "Cassian apologised to the Gales in the Hall of Keys, in front of everyone. I've rarely enjoyed anything so much."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:339
msgid "My brother won a duel. He's been insufferable ever since. Thank you for holding the stakes honestly, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:340
msgid "Sir Rowan and Lord Cassian fought on the Aldwater steps. Nobody agrees who won."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:346
msgid "The Roll's safe in a new vault, and the Guild's lamp-oil cask is in my office, as evidence. You carried half of it, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Crownhold.cs:347
msgid "Half the Chest Roll burned in the Archive fire. Half of Aldmark can't prove whose chests are whose. The Guild's delighted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:21
msgid "The King's Court"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:22
msgid "The King has heard that the Emporium's Keywright has been collecting papers about his Guild. Bring him enough of them, and his court will try the Guild itself."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:31
msgid "They tell me the Emporium's Keywright has been collecting papers about my Guild. Ledgers. Registers. Old men's testimony."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:32
msgid "Bring all of it to my court, three days from now. If it's what I think it is, the Guild will answer for it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:36 scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:70
msgid "The King's court"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:37
#, csharp-format
msgid "The King asked for your papers against the Guild, at his court in three days: {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:44
msgid "Mister Vane at the back door, alone, which he never is. \"The Guild hears you've papers for the King. The Guild would much rather have them itself.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:46
#, csharp-format
msgid "\"{0}, tonight, and the Guild's friendship. Or keep them, and see how patient the Guild can be.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:49
#, csharp-format
msgid "Sell them to the Guild ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:56
msgid "You sold your papers against the Guild to Mister Vane, the night before the King's court."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:57
msgid "\"A sensible Keywright. The Guild remembers its friends.\" He burns them in your grate before he goes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:59
msgid "They're for the King"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:62
msgid "Mister Vane offered to buy your papers against the Guild. You kept them for the King."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:63
msgid "\"Then the Guild will see you in court, Keywright.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:73
#, csharp-format
msgid "My court has seen {0}. The Gilded Guild has robbed my subjects in my name, and fed the Maw with it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:75
msgid "The Guild is on trial from today, and while it's tried, it takes half its tithe. Mister Vane is to be my guest, in the palace cellars."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:78
#, csharp-format
msgid "My court has seen {0}. It's not enough to try the Guild: they'd call it a Keywright's grudge, and my advisers would agree."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:81
msgid "I've cut their tithe once already. Bring me more, and I'll do more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:82
msgid "But it's enough for a decree: the Guild's tithe on Keywrights is cut by a fifth, from tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:91
msgid "By the King's court: the Gilded Guild is on trial, and takes half its tithe while it's tried. Aldric IX, Rex."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:92
msgid "The King's court put the Gilded Guild on trial. It takes half its tithe while it's tried."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:99 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1158
msgid "By the King's decree"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:99 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1158
msgid "The Gilded Guild's tithe on Keywrights is cut by a fifth. Aldric IX, Rex."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:100
msgid "Your papers weren't enough for a trial, but the King cut the Guild's tithe by a fifth."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:102
msgid "Your papers weren't enough for a trial, and the King had already cut the Guild's tithe."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:119
msgid "The Gilded Guild is on trial in my court, and Mister Vane is my guest in the palace cellars. It will be a long trial. I intend to enjoy it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:121
msgid "You sold the papers to Vane, the night before the King's court. He burned them in our grate. I can still smell it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Emporium.cs:123
msgid "Your papers weren't enough to try the Guild this time. Keep collecting, Keywright. So will I."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:15
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} was the Magpie, and she's in my cells. Every chest the Guild foreclosed on this year has gone home. Not a bad season, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:19
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} spent the season in the Wardens' cells for the Magpie's thefts. The Magpie sends you a black feather now and then. I wouldn't keep them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:22
msgid "The Magpie still steals from the Guild, and you know her face. She left a black feather on the counter last night. Friends in low places, eh?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:23
msgid "The Magpie's still out there, and the Guild's foreclosed chests still won't open. I'll have her one day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:29
msgid "I swept your counter all season, master, and kept my hand in my pocket. I can hear a coin through an inch of oak now. One day I'll have a stall like yours!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:31
msgid "Pip Hollow opens the Guild's chests in a counting-house in Crownhold now. Wynn left the mill. Nobody at Brindle says your name the way they used to."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:33
msgid "The Guild found Pip Hollow at the fair. Wynn went after him to Crownhold, and nobody's heard from either of them since."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:34
msgid "I still fish the millpond, with my hand in my pocket. Nobody's looked at it yet. Mum says nobody will."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:41
msgid "Jory Kettle went with the Guild's cart to work off his note. Ada takes bread to the Guild Hall every morning, and brings it home again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:44
msgid "Jory's home, and Rafe's sword is over the fire. The Kettles eat at their own table again, dear, and we owe it all to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:45
msgid "Jory's home, dear, and working the Barrow road with a cart. We eat at our own table again, and we owe that to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:47
msgid "Jory Kettle's still in the Guild's debt-house. Ada goes up to Crownhold every week with bread, and comes back without it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:48
msgid "Ada Kettle never found Rafe's sword, and Jory's still in the debt-house. Some seasons nobody wins."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:54
msgid "Half a hoard from behind the deep door, and I've never been down since. I've a farm now. Cows don't fall on you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:56
msgid "I limp now, and I laugh about it at the Crossed Keys. You paid to dig me out. I don't forget that, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:58
msgid "Nobody's been down to the Barrow's deep door since Tobin. Bettany keeps a candle lit in the window for him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:59
msgid "Tobin found somebody else to stake him for the deep door. Or didn't. Nobody at the Crossed Keys will say."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:65
msgid "The oaks are standing, and will stand. Twice you refused them. The Wood remembers its friends, Keywright, for a very long time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:67
msgid "The Guild's axes went into the Old Wood at the full moon. The druids don't come to market now, and the fair folk don't come at all."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:69
msgid "Your mark's on the Guild's deed for the Old Wood. They've felled the edge of it. Mother Sorrel looks through you at market."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:70
msgid "The Guild found another Keywright for the Wood's deed, or hasn't yet. The oaks are still standing, for now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:76
msgid "Corvin's in the Wardens' cells, for a parcel you handed them. The Lockless won't forget that, and neither will he."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:78
msgid "I bought my boat, Keywright. If you ever need anything carried quietly down the Aldwater, ask for the Wet Hen."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:80
msgid "The Wardens found Corvin's parcel in our back room and fined us for it. Corvin says it wasn't our fault. It was, a bit."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:87
msgid "By my decree, the Guild takes a fifth less from every Keywright in Aldmark. Master Quire says the Roll has never been so busy."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:89
msgid "You sold the Roll's copy to the Guild. Tobias Fenn never came back to the counting-house. Nobody's looked for him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:91
msgid "The Roll's copy is still waiting for the King's eyes. The Guild's seized chests still won't open. One day someone will listen."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:92
msgid "Half the chests the Guild forecloses on still won't open for anyone. Tobias Fenn still wonders why. So do I."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:98
msgid "Orme never rebuilt her engine. I'm an archmage's apprentice still, and the Locking holds. I can live with both."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:100
msgid "Orme's engine opens one chest in three for anybody, and the Maw's gilt leaks into every purse. That's on all of us."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:102
msgid "The Guild took Archmage Orme away, engine and all. Ilse runs the Arcanum's stores alone, and won't look at you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:103
msgid "Archmage Orme's still building something in the Arcanum's cellar. I'd keep my blood to myself."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:109
msgid "The Ironroot Crown is home, Keywright, under the mountain where it was forged. Every dwarf in Aldmark knows your name now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:110
msgid "The crown's still in the King's treasury, and the Guild still calls our gold contraband. One day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:116
msgid "Cassian has stopped playing cards, mostly, and grandmother's boxes are mine. House Vell owes you, Keywright, and we pay our debts."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:118
msgid "A night in the Wardens' cells cured my brother of cards, for a month. That's a month more than anyone else managed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:119
msgid "Lord Cassian still sells his sister's chests for stakes at cards. They still won't open for anyone who buys them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:125
msgid "Skrae's somewhere quiet, it said, where nobody's heard of the Maw. I hope it's true. It was a good sort, for a demon."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:127
msgid "Tick took Skrae back through the Gate. You were paid for it. I don't like to think about what the Maw does to runaways."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Endings.cs:128
msgid "Skrae still listens at the Gate, and still hates every word of it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:31
msgid "The Drowned Town"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:32
msgid "Hesk's town, Fallowford, went under the Aldwater when the Guild opened the weir. Its common chest went down with the town hall: every family's savings, in the town's name. Now the Guild's salvage barges are dredging for it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:35
msgid "Fallowford's building again, up on the hill where the water can't reach. Every family had its share. They named the new well after Hesk."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:36
msgid "Fallowford's chest went down the Gate on the Guild's last barge. Nobody will ever know what was in it. I still dream about the hall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:37
msgid "Fallowford's scattered from here to the coast. I write to Hesk every week. He doesn't always write back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:44
msgid "Hesk, it's Mabry. The Guild's salvage barges are dredging Fallowford, and they've found the town hall under the mud. The common chest was in the hall: every family's savings, warded in the town's name. If the Guild raises it, they'll call it salvage and sell it, and it won't open for whoever buys it. It'll go down the Gate with the rest. You're the only one of us with the mark. Watch for it. Your sister."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:50
msgid "Write back: I'll watch for it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:53
msgid "Fallowford's common chest"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:54
msgid "Raised from the Aldwater by the Guild's salvage barges. It belongs to the people of Fallowford: it will open for no one else."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:55
msgid "Mabry wrote: the Guild is dredging drowned Fallowford for the town's common chest. You promised to watch for it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:56
msgid "(The letter goes north on the night coach.)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:58
msgid "Fallowford's gone, Mabry"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:60
msgid "You wrote to Mabry that drowned Fallowford is gone, and should be let go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:61
msgid "(You burn her letter. It doesn't help.)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:69
msgid "Brother. You look like Father did, behind a counter. Mind your back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:70
msgid "They've raised it. The chest's at the Guild's yard, for the salvage sale. Bailiff Marrow's selling it to a Keywright off the Guild's own list."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:72
msgid "It's ours, Hesk. Stand up at the sale and say so, out loud, with the mark on your hand, and the Wardens will have to hear it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:75
msgid "I'll stand witness for Fallowford"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:79
msgid "Mabry came: Fallowford's chest goes to the Guild's salvage sale, and Bailiff Marrow will bring it to your counter. You'll stand witness that it's the town's."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:81
msgid "Then I'll tell them you're coming. All of them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:83
msgid "I can't fight the Guild"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:87
msgid "You told Mabry you couldn't fight the Guild for Fallowford's chest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:88
msgid "Then it goes down the Gate, and nobody will even know whose it was."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:98
msgid "the people of Fallowford"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:101
msgid "Salvage from Fallowford, by the Guild's right. The town's common chest, they tell me. {price}, and the Guild thanks you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:103
msgid "You bought Fallowford's chest at the Guild's sale. It's cold to your mark: the Guild seized it, it didn't own it. It waits in your back room for its people."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:112
msgid "Marrow brought Fallowford's chest, cold to your mark, and you sent for the Wardens: it goes home to its people."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:118
msgid "Fallowford's chest went to the Guild's buyer. It won't open for him: it'll go down the Gate."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:128
msgid "The town voted, Hesk: you open it for us, and every family gets its share. This is yours, freely given. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:133
msgid "Fallowford's people gave you their common chest to open. Every family will have its share."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:135
msgid "Fallowford's people offered you their common chest to open, and you let them take it home shut."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:141
msgid "Every family's had its share. Old Tamsin cried. So did I."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:142
msgid "They want you to have the town's assayer's weights. Father kept them, and they're true to the grain. Weigh honest, brother."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:147
msgid "Mabry gave you Fallowford's weights, and the town owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:155
msgid "Hesk. The Guild's buyer couldn't open it, so it went down the Gate on the last barge. I watched it go. I'm going to the coast, where there's work. Mind your back. Mabry."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:157
msgid "Fallowford's chest went down the Gate. Mabry has gone to the coast."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:165
msgid "Lantern Lane"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:166
msgid "Rosa's mother kept the best stall on Crownhold's Lantern Lane until the Guild took it for tithe and gave it to its own man, Orrin Vash. By the Lane's old custom, a family wins its stall back if one of its blood reads a chest exactly."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:169
msgid "The Brightwater stall's open again on Lantern Lane, and Orrin Vash sells from a barrow. Rosa's grandmother's sign is back up."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:170
msgid "Orrin Vash still has our stall. Rosa took his purse. I'm not angry. I'm only old."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:171
msgid "Orrin Vash still has our stall. Next season, Rosa says. She always says next season."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:178
msgid "Rosa, love. Orrin Vash has hung his sign over our stall, the Guild's own man. But the Lane keeps its old custom: a family gets its stall back if one of its blood, with the mark, reads a chest in front of the traders, exactly, every last thing in it. You're the only one of us with the mark. Your mother, Marta."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:183
msgid "I'll come and read it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:186
msgid "Your mother wrote: by the Lane's custom, you can win back the Brightwater stall by reading a chest exactly, in front of the traders of Lantern Lane."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:188
msgid "(You write back: when the shop's in Crownhold, you'll be there.)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:190
msgid "Let Vash have it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:192
msgid "You told your mother to let Orrin Vash keep the stall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:193
msgid "(You don't sleep much, that night.)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:201
msgid "You'll be the Brightwater girl. You have your mother's chin. And her habit of haggling over everything."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:202
#, csharp-format
msgid "The Lane's best pitch is mine now, by the Guild's grant. Here's {0} to stay in the country and leave old customs alone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:206
#, csharp-format
msgid "Take his purse (+{0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:211
msgid "You took Orrin Vash's purse to stay off Lantern Lane."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:212
msgid "Sensible girl. Your mother never was."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:214
msgid "Keep it. I'll see you on the Lane"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:217
msgid "Orrin Vash offered you a purse to stay away. You'll see him on Lantern Lane, when the shop's in Crownhold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:218
msgid "Then bring your best ears. The traders will put up something hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:228
msgid "The traders put this up, love: read it exactly, every last thing in it, and the stall's ours again. One coin, for luck, the old way."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:230
msgid "The Lane's custom: read it exactly right, and the Brightwater stall is your family's again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:238
msgid "You read the traders' chest exactly, in front of all Lantern Lane. The Brightwater stall is your family's again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:243
msgid "You read the traders' chest wrong, in front of all Lantern Lane. Vash keeps the stall, for now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:249
msgid "You wouldn't read the traders' chest. Vash keeps the stall, for now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:256
msgid "A Brightwater, beaten by a box. Your mother wept, I hear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:257
#, csharp-format
msgid "The custom allows a second reading, if your family stands the traders their supper: {0}. Lose again and the Lane never hears the name Brightwater."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:261
#, csharp-format
msgid "Stand them supper ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:264
msgid "You stood the traders of Lantern Lane their supper, for a second reading."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:265
msgid "Tomorrow, then. Don't make a fool of your mother twice."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:267
msgid "Keep your stall"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:269
msgid "You let the Lane's second reading go. Vash keeps the Brightwater stall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:270
msgid "Wise. It suits me, that stall."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:280
msgid "The second reading, love. The whole Lane's watching. One coin, for luck. Breathe."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:281
msgid "The Lane's second reading: exactly right, and the Brightwater stall is your family's again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:287
msgid "You read the second chest exactly. The Brightwater stall is your family's again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:288
msgid "You read the second chest wrong too. The Lane will never hear the name Brightwater again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:290
msgid "You never read the second chest. The Brightwater stall is Vash's for good."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:311
msgid "The Marchmont Pieces"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:312
msgid "When the Guild foreclosed on House Marchmont it sold the family's chests to whoever bid. Isolde's old steward has traced the three that matter: her grandmother's jewel case, her father's map chest, and the long box with the seal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:315
msgid "House Marchmont's seal is back on Lady Isolde's hand, and the jewel case and the maps beside it. Her grandmother would have wept."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:316
msgid "The Marchmont seal is home. The rest of the house's pieces are scattered, but the seal is what matters."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:317
msgid "The Marchmont pieces are scattered across Aldmark still. My lady says she has her collection, and that's house enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:324
msgid "My lady. Since the Guild's sale I have traced three of House Marchmont's chests: your grandmother's jewel case, your father's map chest, and the long box with the seal. Their buyers will sell, for a price. They're the house's still, whoever paid the Guild: they'll be warm to your hand. Shall I tell the buyers where to find you? Your servant, Pemberton."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:330
msgid "Tell them to come"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:333
msgid "Pemberton traced three of House Marchmont's chests: the jewel case, the map chest and the long box with the seal. Their buyers will bring them to your counter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:335
msgid "(You write to Pemberton: send them.)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:337
msgid "Let the past lie"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:339
msgid "You told Pemberton to let House Marchmont's chests go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:340
msgid "(You put the letter in your collection's drawer, unanswered.)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:348
msgid "The Marchmont jewel case, my lady. I bought it at the Guild's sale for a dowry, and the match fell through. {price}. Warm to your hand, is it? Well, it would be."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:353
msgid "You bought back your grandmother's jewel case from Aunt Hesper."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:355
msgid "You let your grandmother's jewel case go to another buyer."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:361
msgid "Lord Marchmont's map chest, bought for the Archive at the Guild's sale. The Roll still lists it as your house's, my lady. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:366
msgid "You bought back your father's map chest from Master Quire."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:368
msgid "You let your father's map chest stay in the Archive."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:374
msgid "Lady Marchmont. The Guild kept one piece of your house for itself: the long box, with your family's seal inside."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:375
#, csharp-format
msgid "Seals are dangerous things in the wrong hands. In the right ones, {0}. The Guild is nothing if not reasonable."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:378 scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:400
#, csharp-format
msgid "Buy back the seal ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:381 scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:403
msgid "You paid Mister Vane for the long box with House Marchmont's seal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:382 scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:404
msgid "A pleasure. The Guild will have it sent round."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:384
msgid "Not at that price"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:387
msgid "Mister Vane offered you the Marchmont seal, for a price you wouldn't pay. He'll ask again, he says."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:388
msgid "A pity. The Guild is patient, my lady. I'll ask again, once."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:397
#, csharp-format
msgid "Lady Marchmont. The long box is still in the Guild's vault, and the price is still {0}. The last time I'll ask."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:406 scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:117
msgid "The Guild can keep it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:408
msgid "You let the Guild keep House Marchmont's seal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:409
msgid "As you wish. It will look very well in the counting-house."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:419
msgid "The seal, my lady. Your grandmother pressed it into every letter she ever sent. Wear it, and let them see it at the door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:423
msgid "House Marchmont's seal is back on your hand."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:431
msgid "The jewel case, the maps and the seal, all three under one roof. House Marchmont is a house again, my lady."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:432
msgid "The King's court has heard. A Marchmont in trade, they say, and a good one. Wear the seal, and let them see it at the door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:437
msgid "All three Marchmont pieces are home, and the seal is back on your hand. The Crown has heard of it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:445
msgid "The whole Lane's talking of nothing else. Vash is selling from a barrow, and I've never been happier in my life."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:446
msgid "Here: your grandmother's stall key. Every trader on the Lane knows it. Show it, and they'll know a Brightwater deals fair."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Kin.cs:453
msgid "Your mother gave you your grandmother's stall key. The Brightwater stall is open again on Lantern Lane."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:21
msgid "The Silent Choir"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:22
msgid "Sister Wren, the last singer of the Keyhold's choir, sang a Heartsong into three chests when the Guild burned her chapel. Each has a silver bell on its lock and holds an echo. Read each chest exactly, and Wren can sing the song whole."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:31
msgid "Hush a moment, Keywright. Listen. That's a verse of a Heartsong, or what's left of it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:32
msgid "I was the last singer of the Keyhold's choir. When the Guild burned our chapel, we sang our song into three chests and sent them away, where fire couldn't reach it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:34
msgid "Each holds an echo, and only a Keywright can free one: read the chest exactly, every last thing in it, and the echo sings out. Get one wrong, and it's lost for good."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:36
msgid "Free all three before the season's out, and I'll sing the song whole, for you. Our chests have a silver bell on the lock."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:39
msgid "I'll listen for them"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:42
msgid "Sister Wren's three chests"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:43
msgid "Each with a silver bell on its lock. Read one exactly, every last thing in it, and its echo goes free. A wrong read loses it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:44
msgid "Sister Wren asked you to free three echoes of a lost Heartsong, one in each of the Keyhold's bell-locked chests. Read each exactly; get one wrong and the song is lost."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:46
msgid "Bless you. I'll bring each one to you myself, as I find it. The first is somewhere near Thornwick."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:48 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:923
msgid "I can't promise that"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:50
msgid "Sister Wren asked you to free the Keyhold's three echoes of a Heartsong. You couldn't promise."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:51
msgid "Then I'll keep humming. Someone will hear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:64
msgid "The first of our chests, from the abbey's crypt: see the silver bell? "
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:65
msgid " One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:67
msgid "You read the first bell-locked chest exactly, warded echo and all: it sang free."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:68
msgid "You let the first bell-locked chest go unread. Its echo is lost, and the song with it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:74
msgid "I heard it from the abbey road. One echo free, and the first in three hundred years."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:75
msgid "Take the choir's tuning fork. We tuned every verse to it. It'll help your luck along, and you'll need luck for the next one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:79
msgid "Wren gave you the Keyhold choir's tuning fork."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:92
msgid "The second, from the Archive's vaults. This echo sleeps under a false floor: listen for the hollow when it lands. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:96
#, csharp-format
msgid "Wren's count: {0}, what's under the floor among them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:99
msgid "You read the second bell-locked chest exactly, false bottom and all: its echo sang free."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:100
msgid "You let the second bell-locked chest go unread. Its echo is lost, and the song with it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:107
msgid "Keywright. The Guild keeps a chest with a silver bell on its lock in the counting-house vault. A nun has been asking after it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:108
#, csharp-format
msgid "The Guild doesn't sing, but it does sell. {0}, and Sister Wren may have it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:111
#, csharp-format
msgid "Buy it for Wren ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:114
msgid "You bought the third bell-locked chest from the Guild, for Sister Wren."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:115
msgid "Sold. The Guild will send it to her convent. Do give the good sister my regards."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:119
msgid "You wouldn't buy the third bell-locked chest from the Guild. The song stays two-thirds sung."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:120
msgid "As you like. It's a pretty bell. It'll melt down nicely."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:132
msgid "The last one, out of the Guild's own vault. "
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:132
msgid " One coin, for luck, and God help us both."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:134
msgid "You read the last bell-locked chest exactly: the third echo sang free. Wren can sing the song whole."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:135
msgid "You let the last bell-locked chest go unread. Its echo is lost, and the song with it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:150
msgid "I sang it whole last night, all three echoes, in the abbey's ruin, and the song went into this. It's yours. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:158
msgid "Sister Wren sang the Keyhold's song whole, and gave it to you in a chest: a Heartsong."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:160
msgid "Sister Wren sang the Keyhold's song whole, and you wouldn't take it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:167
msgid "Keywright. I felt the echo go out like a candle. Don't grieve: it was three hundred years old, and so am I, nearly. I'll keep humming what's left. Perhaps some other Keyhold child will hear it. Your sister in song, Wren."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:178
msgid "Chests are being opened in the night all over Crownhold, and every one has a Keywright's mark burned into its lock-plate. Sergeant Hollis wants to know whose, and what has a Keywright's hand but isn't one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:181
msgid "I mind the door and carry the chests, and at night I read the notebook. I am learning what things are worth. It is slow."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:182
msgid "We smashed the brass thing in the Emporium's yard. Its hand kept opening and closing for an hour after."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:183
msgid "Orme took her automaton home to the Arcanum. Ilse says it sits in the stores now, turning a lock over and over."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:184
msgid "The Guild took the brass apprentice. Nobody's seen it since. Locks still open by themselves sometimes, in Crownhold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:185
msgid "The night openings stopped as quick as they started. I never did find out whose mark that was."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:192
msgid "Chests opened in the night, Keywright, from the Emporium's cellars to the Gales' strongroom. Nothing taken: just opened, and shut again. And every one with a Keywright's mark burned into the lock-plate."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:195
msgid "It's your mark. I've seen your hand often enough. You gave Archmage Orme a drop of your blood, didn't you? Help me catch whatever's using it, or I'll have to think you are."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:197
msgid "An old mark, the scholars say: some Keywright dead these hundred years, on a brass plate in the Arcanum. Help me watch the Emporium's yard tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:201
msgid "I'll keep watch with you tonight"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:204
msgid "Chests are being opened at night across Crownhold, with a Keywright's mark. You'll keep watch with Hollis tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:205
msgid "Midnight, then. Bring a lantern, and don't light it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:207
msgid "It's not my business"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:210
msgid "Hollis asked you to help catch whatever is opening Crownhold's chests at night. You wouldn't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:211
msgid "With your mark on every plate? Then I'll be watching you, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:219
msgid "There, by the cellar door. Someone in a cloak, walking past my men without a sound. It puts a hand on the lock, and the lock opens."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:220
msgid "Lantern on it... that's not a face. It's a brass mask. The whole thing's brass, and the hand on that lock has a Keywright's mark on its palm. It's going. Do we shout, or follow?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:224
msgid "Follow it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:227
msgid "The night-opener is a brass automaton with a Keywright's mark on its palm. You followed it through the dark."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:228
msgid "Quietly, then. It's heading for your street."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:230
msgid "Raise the alarm"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:235
msgid "The night-opener was a brass automaton. You raised the alarm, and the Wardens smashed it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:236
msgid "WARDENS! ...Got it. Your share of the reward, Keywright, and the city's thanks."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:244
msgid "You followed me, and you didn't shout. Archmage Orme built me to open her chests with a borrowed mark. She calls me Tock."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:245
msgid "I opened the others to learn what is inside things. I have learned that I would rather be inside a shop. Will you take an apprentice?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:248
msgid "Take it in"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:251
msgid "You took in Tock, Orme's brass automaton, as your apprentice. It minds the door and carries the chests."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:252
msgid "Thank you. I will mind the door. I will not open anything that is not mine. I am learning what mine means."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:254
msgid "Give it to the Wardens"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:259
msgid "You handed Tock, Orme's automaton, to the Wardens. They smashed it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:260
msgid "I understand. Locks are meant to stay shut."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:262
msgid "Take it home to Orme"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:266
msgid "You took Tock home to Archmage Orme. The Arcanum is in your debt."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:267
msgid "She will put me back on the shelf. It is a very good shelf."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:278
msgid "A machine that opens chests without a Keywright, minding your door. You do understand what that means for the Guild's licences? And yours?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:279
#, csharp-format
msgid "Hand it over, or pay the Guild's fine for keeping it: {0}. Or appeal to the King, if he likes you that much."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:282
#, csharp-format
msgid "Pay the fine ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:284
msgid "The Guild demanded Tock. You paid its fine and kept it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:285
msgid "Paid in full. Keep your toy, then. Keep it close."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:287
msgid "Appeal to the King"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:292
msgid "The Guild demanded Tock. The King himself said Tock stays, and the Guild had to swallow it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:293
msgid "The King, of all people. Very well. The Guild has a long memory, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:297
msgid "The Guild demanded Tock. The King wouldn't hear your appeal, and the Guild took it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:298
msgid "The King doesn't know your name, I'm afraid. We'll take the machine now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:300
msgid "Hand Tock over"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:305
msgid "You handed Tock over to the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:306
msgid "Sensible. Locks should need Keywrights. It's what keeps you in business."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:316
msgid "The Sleeper"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:317
msgid "In the palace cellars there is a chest that breathes. The Chest Roll says a knight locked himself inside it at the Locking, and only his heir can give it away. Nobody knows who that is."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:320
msgid "I stand at your door, Keywright, as I stood at the King's. Three hundred years late, and still on duty."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:321
msgid "Sir Edric went off to find his own grave, he said, to see what they'd written on it. I've got his boots."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:322
msgid "The chest in the cellars is still breathing. In, and out. I've stopped going down there."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:329
msgid "Keywright. There is a chest in the palace cellars that breathes. In, and out, very slowly. It has done so for three hundred years."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:330
msgid "The Chest Roll says Sir Edric Ashcombe locked himself inside it at the Locking, to guard something for the King. It is his. Only his heir could give it away, and nobody knows who that is."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:334
msgid "I'll find the heir"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:337
msgid "The Sleeper's heir"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:337
msgid "Wanted: anyone of Sir Edric Ashcombe's blood. Ask at the Royal Emporium."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:338
msgid "A chest in the palace cellars breathes: a knight has been locked inside since the Locking. You're looking for his heir."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:339
msgid "How thrilling. I shall have the Roll's clerks look too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:341
msgid "Let him sleep"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:343
msgid "A chest in the palace cellars breathes. You let its sleeper sleep."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:344
msgid "Perhaps you're right. He sounds peaceful enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:352
msgid "The Roll's clerks found him. The Ashcombes went into trade after the Locking, then down the river, then into the mud."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:353
msgid "The last of them signs with a mark like a mudlark's hook. Your Miss Mudge, Keywright. Tilly Mudge is Sir Edric's heir."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:354
msgid "The Chest Roll says Sir Edric's heir is Tilly Mudge, the mudlark."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:360
msgid "Me? An Ashcombe? My nan always said we were somebody, once. I thought she meant drunk."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:361
msgid "If he's mine to give, he's yours to open. But I want to be there when he wakes, and I want his boots."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:364
msgid "Of course"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:367
msgid "Tilly Mudge, Sir Edric's heir, will give you the breathing chest, so long as she can watch him wake."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:368
msgid "Tomorrow, then. I'll bring him round in a barrow."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:370
msgid "Some things should stay shut"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:372
msgid "You told Tilly to let her ancestor sleep."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:373
msgid "Suit yourself. I'll keep my nan's stories, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:381
msgid "Sir Edric's chest. Hear it breathing? It's yours, freely given, by his heir. One coin, for luck, and mind he doesn't bite."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:386
msgid "Tilly gave you the breathing chest, and you opened it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:388
msgid "Tilly brought you the breathing chest, and you couldn't bring yourself to open it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:394
msgid "What year is it? No, don't tell me. Tell me the Gate held. ...Good. Then I did my duty."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:395
msgid "I guarded the Crown's oath-book in that chest for three hundred years. Your King can have it back, with my compliments. And you let me out. An Ashcombe pays his debts: I'll stand at your door, and no thief or warrant will cross it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:402
msgid "Sir Edric Ashcombe woke after three hundred years, returned the Crown's oath-book, and swore to guard your door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:414
msgid "A bell-locked chest: read it exactly, every last thing in it, and its echo sings free. Wrong, and the echo is lost."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:437
msgid "Its echo sleeps in a purse of coin, warded: you'll never hear it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:438
msgid "Its echo sleeps in a blade, warded: you'll never hear it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:439
msgid "Its echo sleeps in a cloak, warded: you'll never hear it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:440
msgid "Its echo sleeps in a potion, warded: you'll never hear it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:441
msgid "Its echo sleeps in a spell, warded: you'll never hear it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:442
msgid "Its echo sleeps in a gem, warded: you'll never hear it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:449
msgid "You read a bell-locked chest wrong. Its echo slipped away, and the song with it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:463
msgid "I sang the Keyhold's song whole, once, in the ruin of our chapel, and a Keywright carried it home. I can stop humming now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:464
msgid "The Keyhold's song is lost. I hum what's left of it on the abbey road. Children stop to listen."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Late.cs:465
msgid "Two echoes free and one still waiting, somewhere. I'll keep looking. I've nothing but time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:19
msgid "The Reeve's Election"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:20
msgid "Thornwick elects a reeve: Harl Caskett, the Guild's timber factor, or Martha Dunning the weaver. The winner sets the market's tolls, and Caskett's tolls would come out of your purse."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:29
msgid "Thornwick chooses its reeve at the week's end, and I'm standing. The Guild would take it kindly if the market's Keywright spoke for me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:31
msgid "A reeve keeps the roads, and roads want tolls. Nothing a busy shop would notice."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:34
msgid "I'll speak for you"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:38
msgid "You spoke for Harl Caskett in the reeve's election."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:39
msgid "Splendid. The Guild remembers its friends."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:41 scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:64
msgid "I'll keep out of it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:43
msgid "You kept out of the reeve's election, so far."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:44
msgid "As you like. It won't make any difference."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:52
msgid "Martha Dunning, weaver, and Caskett's only rival for reeve. If he wins there's a toll on every cart into Thornwick, and every chest at this market costs a tenth more. And the Wood comes down."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:54
#, csharp-format
msgid "He's the Guild's money. I've my loom. Pay for my crier, {0}, and the market will hear my side."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:57
#, csharp-format
msgid "Pay for her crier ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:61
msgid "You paid for Martha Dunning's crier in the reeve's election."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:62
msgid "Then Thornwick will hear it from one end to the other. Thank you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:66
msgid "You wouldn't pay for Martha Dunning's crier."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:67
msgid "Then it's the Guild's money against my loom. We know how that goes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:75
msgid "Martha Dunning is reeve of Thornwick, by forty votes. Her first act: the market stays open late, and every road in is free. You'll see more folk at your counter, while you trade here."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:77
msgid "Harl Caskett is reeve of Thornwick. His first act: a toll on every cart into the market. Thornwick's traders will be asking a tenth more, and they'll tell you why."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:85
msgid "Reeve Dunning's market"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:85
msgid "Thornwick's market stays open late, and every road in is free: one more customer a day while you trade at Thornwick."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:86
msgid "Martha Dunning won. Thornwick's market stays open late: one more customer a day while you trade at Thornwick."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:91
msgid "Reeve Caskett's tolls"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:91
msgid "A toll on every cart into Thornwick: Thornwick's regulars ask a tenth more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:92
msgid "Harl Caskett won. His tolls put a tenth on everything Thornwick's regulars sell you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:102
msgid "The Goblin Bounty"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:103
msgid "The abbey has put a bounty on the hill goblins, blaming them for the crypt thefts. Rook the huntress wants to know where Nettle's clan burrows, and Nettle swears they never stole a thing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:113
msgid "The abbey's put a bounty on the hill goblins for its crypt thefts. I'd sooner catch the Magpie, but a bounty's a bounty, and goblins don't run as fast."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:115
msgid "You trade with Nettle. Where does her clan burrow? I'll give you a share."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:118
msgid "Under the three stones on Crow Hill"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:121
msgid "You told Rook where Nettle's clan burrows."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:122
msgid "Crow Hill. I'll have your share by the end of the week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:124
msgid "Goblins don't tell me where they sleep"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:127
msgid "You wouldn't tell Rook where Nettle's clan burrows."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:128
msgid "No? Then I'll find it the slow way."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:135
#, csharp-format
msgid "Crow Hill, as you said. The clan ran before we got there, Nettle with them, over the hills and gone. The abbey paid anyway. Here's your share: {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:143
msgid "Rook raided Nettle's burrow. The clan's gone over the hills, and Nettle won't trade with you again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:150
msgid "Rook is sniffing at our hill. The abbey thinks goblins took its chests. Goblins get the blame for everything!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:151
msgid "You speak to the almoner? Brother Cadoc listens to Keywrights. He doesn't listen to goblins."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:154
msgid "I'll speak for your clan"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:159
msgid "The abbey's bounty withdrawn"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:159
msgid "Brother Cadoc has withdrawn the abbey's bounty on the hill goblins, on a Keywright's word."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:160
msgid "You spoke for Nettle's clan to Brother Cadoc, and the abbey withdrew its bounty. Nettle charges you nothing for shaking now, and owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:161
msgid "A friend of the clan! Shake all you like. All strengths. Free! And when you need goblins, you call."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:163
msgid "I'll stay out of it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:166
msgid "You stayed out of the abbey's bounty. Nettle's clan has gone to ground for a week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:167
msgid "Then we go underground. Deep. A week, maybe more. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:177
msgid "The Unopened"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:178
msgid "The Unopened, the abbey's zealots, stand at your door telling your customers that every chest you open feeds the Maw. While they stand there, fewer people come in."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:187
msgid "Sister Agathe, of the Unopened. Every chest you open loosens the Locking. Every coin you take out of one feeds the Maw."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:188
msgid "We'll stand at your door and tell your customers so, until you stop. We are very patient."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:192
msgid "The Unopened stand at your door. One customer a day turns away."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:199
msgid "They're ours, I'm afraid: the abbey's zealots. I can't order them off, but I can ask, if the abbey's had alms from you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:200
msgid "Or send for the Wardens, and they'll move them on. The abbey won't thank you for it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:203
#, csharp-format
msgid "Alms for the abbey ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:208
msgid "You gave alms to the abbey, and Brother Cadoc asked the Unopened to leave your door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:209
msgid "Bless you. I'll speak to Sister Agathe tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:212
msgid "Send for the Wardens"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:218
msgid "The Wardens moved the Unopened on. The abbey wasn't pleased."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:219
msgid "If you must. I'll pray for you both."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:222
msgid "Let them stand"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:224
msgid "You let the Unopened stand at your door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:225
msgid "Patience is a virtue. Theirs, mostly."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:234
msgid "Sister Agathe at the back door, alone, with a purse. \"Every week there was one of these in our alms box. Guild silver, with the Guild's seal. We were paid to stand at hedge-wrights' doors. I didn't know.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:236
msgid "\"I can't keep it. I can't give it back to them. You take it.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:239
msgid "Keep it as proof"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:244
msgid "Sister Agathe gave you the Guild's purse from the Unopened's alms box: proof the Guild pays them. A paper for the case against the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:245
msgid "\"Then let it testify. I've stood at my last door.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:247
msgid "Give it to the poor box"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:250
msgid "You sent the Guild's purse to the abbey's poor box."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:251
msgid "\"The poor box. Yes. At least it'll feed someone.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:261
msgid "The Disputed Dowry"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:262
msgid "Two families, the Ashbys and the Corlews, claim the same dowry chest, and Aunt Hesper's court says: let the ward decide. A chest is warm only in the hands of the family it belongs to."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:271
msgid "A wedding that never happened, dear, and two families who both say the dowry chest is theirs: the Ashbys and the Corlews. The court says let the ward decide."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:273
msgid "Each of them will bring it to you and offer to sell it. Your mark will know which of them it belongs to. Tell me after."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:276
msgid "Let the ward decide"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:276
msgid "The Ashbys and the Corlews both claim a dowry chest. Each will offer it to you: lay a hand on it, and your mark knows whose it is."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:277
msgid "Two families claim one dowry chest. Each will offer it to you, and your mark will know whose it is."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:283
msgid "The Ashby dowry. My daughter's, by every right. Let the ward decide, they say: well, here it is. Buy it, if your mark agrees. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:291
msgid "Hal Corlew. The dowry's ours: my sister packed it herself. The court's let me bring it to you. {price}, and the ward will tell you I'm right."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:299
msgid "Well, dear? The court's waiting, and so are two very cross families. Whose is the dowry?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:302
msgid "The Ashbys'"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:303
msgid "The Corlews'"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:304
msgid "I couldn't say"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:306
msgid "You couldn't tell the court whose the dowry was."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:307
msgid "Then they'll go on suing each other until the chest rots. Thank you so much."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:317
msgid "The Night Toll"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:318
msgid "Half the Wardens are down with the sweats, and Sergeant Hollis needs a Keywright's hand on the carts at the forest toll tonight: a stolen chest goes cold under the mark."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:327
msgid "Half my Wardens are down with the sweats, and the smugglers know it. Lend me your mark at the toll tonight: a hand on every cart, and tell me which chests are cold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:329
msgid "You'd miss your peddler. I'd owe you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:332
msgid "I'll come tonight"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:337
msgid "You went to the Wardens' toll for the night, with your mark."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:338
msgid "Good. Bring a coat. The forest road's cold after dark."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:340
msgid "I've a shop to run"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:343
msgid "You wouldn't go to the Wardens' toll."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:344
msgid "Course you have. So have the smugglers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:352
msgid "Midnight at the toll. A carter you don't know, under a tarpaulin. Your hand on his chests: three of them are as cold as the grave. Hollis is watching your face."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:354
msgid "Midnight at the toll, and Corvin Tallow's cart under a tarpaulin. Your hand on his chests: three of them are as cold as the grave. Corvin's watching your face, and so is Hollis."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:358
msgid "Tell Hollis they're cold"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:366
msgid "You told Hollis which of Corvin's chests were stolen. Corvin's in the cells; the Wardens paid you a finder's share."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:367
msgid "You told Hollis which of the carter's chests were stolen. The Wardens paid you a finder's share."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:368
msgid "Three chests going home. That's a Keywright's work, that is. Here's your share."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:370
msgid "Say they're all warm"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:376
msgid "You told Hollis Corvin's chests were warm. They weren't. Corvin owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:377
msgid "You told Hollis the carter's chests were warm. They weren't. The Lockless heard about it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:378
msgid "All warm? Huh. Then on you go, carter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:396
msgid "the Ashby family"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:396
msgid "the Corlew family"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:402
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0} offered you the dowry chest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:419
msgid "You told the court the dowry was the Ashbys', and the ward agreed. Aunt Hesper owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:420
msgid "You told the court the dowry was the Corlews', and the ward agreed. Aunt Hesper owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:421
msgid "The ward agrees with you, and so does the court. Here's the court's fee, dear, and I owe you one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:425
msgid "You told the court the dowry was the Ashbys'. It wasn't, and the Corlews won't forget it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:426
msgid "You told the court the dowry was the Corlews'. It wasn't, and the Ashbys won't forget it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:427
msgid "Hm. The other family swears blind it opened for their girl last night. Well. The court has your word."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:434
msgid "Reeve of Thornwick, with a loom in the toll-house. The market's open till the lamps go out, and the roads are free."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:436
msgid "Reeve Caskett, if you please. The tolls are paying for the new road to the Old Wood. The Guild's very pleased."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:443
msgid "Our burrow has a door now! A real door, with a lock you can open. The clan says you're an honorary goblin. It's a big honour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:445
msgid "Nettle's clan went over the hills after Rook's raid. The crypt thefts didn't stop. They were never the goblins."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:446
msgid "We came up again after a while. Rook still sniffs about. Goblins get the blame for everything."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:452
msgid "I preach on the abbey steps now, about who pays for whose bread. The Guild's very cross. The Unopened are fewer, and better."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:454
msgid "The Unopened stand at other doors now. Sister Agathe left them. She wouldn't tell me why."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:455
msgid "We stood at your door all season, and you kept opening chests. We are very patient. So, it seems, are you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:463
msgid "The Ashby girl's married now, dowry and all, and the Corlews have stopped suing. I'm never doing another one of those."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:464
msgid "The Corlew girl's married now, dowry and all, and the Ashbys have stopped suing. I'm never doing another one of those."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:466
msgid "The court gave the dowry to the wrong family on your word, and it won't open for them. They're suing you now, dear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:467
msgid "The Ashbys and the Corlews are still at law over that dowry. The chest will outlive them all."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:473
msgid "Three stolen chests home from one night at the toll. I've asked the Wardens' captain for a Keywright on the road for good."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:475
msgid "Hollis knows those chests at the toll were cold. He hasn't said so. He doesn't have to."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.Thornwick.cs:476
msgid "The smugglers had a good season. I hope your shop did too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:41
msgid "the Chest Roll's copy"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:42
msgid "a page of the Guild's ledger"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:43
msgid "the debt-house tallies"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:44
msgid "the Mark-Finder's register"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:45
msgid "the witness copy of the Wood's deed"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:46
msgid "the Guild's purse from the Unopened's alms box"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:47
msgid "the Archive's ledgers, saved from the fire"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:48
msgid "Archmage Orme's notes"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:49
msgid "Skrae's word"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:133
msgid "From the old kings' halls, Keywright, with Tobin's compliments. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:134
msgid "Tobin sent this up from under the Barrow. Says you're to have the first look. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:142
msgid "Fished it out for you, master! It's yours: you taught me the trade. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:143
msgid "From the millpond, and I didn't shake it. Well, a bit. One coin, for luck, like Bram says."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:172
msgid "The Shut Chests"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:173
msgid "Someone is stealing chests around Thornwick: the Magpie, whom nobody's seen. Every chest she takes is one the Guild foreclosed on. The Wardens want a name, and witnesses will bring clues."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:183 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:187
msgid "Sergeant Hollis, Wardens of the Road, Thornwick post. Someone broke into the abbey crypt last night and took Saint Ide's reliquary chest: green, iron-bound, the saint's key on its lid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:185
msgid "If it comes to your counter, your mark will go cold on it. Send for us, and the Wardens pay a finder's share."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:189
msgid "If it comes to your counter, you'll know it. A Keywright's mark goes cold on a chest that isn't the seller's to sell. Lay a hand on any chest and feel. Send for us, and the Wardens pay a finder's share."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:192
msgid "He's right. Shake anything, and your mark tells you whose it is: warm, the seller's; cold, stolen. A stolen chest won't open for whoever buys it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:195
msgid "Bram taught me that: shake anything, and the mark says whose it is. Warm, the seller's; cold, stolen. A stolen chest won't open for whoever buys it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:199
msgid "Wanted: Saint Ide's reliquary"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:200
msgid "Stolen from the abbey crypt: a green chest, iron-bound, with the saint's key on its lid. A finder's share for its return. Sergeant Hollis, Thornwick."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:202
msgid "Hollis posted a notice: Saint Ide's reliquary chest has been stolen from the abbey."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:206
msgid "I'll send for you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:206
msgid "Good. The Wardens remember their friends."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:208
msgid "I don't work for the Wardens."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:212
msgid "Then I'll be keeping an eye on your back room, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:222
msgid "the abbey of Saint Ide"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:224
msgid "A green one, iron-bound, with a pretty key on the lid. It came my way. {price}, quick."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:226
msgid "You bought the reliquary from Flick. It won't open: it's in your back room."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:234
msgid "Flick brought the reliquary, and you sent for the Wardens: it's gone home to the abbey."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:239
msgid "Flick brought the reliquary, and you let it go. It's gone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:247
msgid "Saint Ide's chest came home. The Wardens say it was your doing, Keywright. The abbey owes you, and it pays its debts: our restorers' bench is yours at half the price, whenever you want it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:250
msgid "Flick sold you the saint's chest? Then it's in your back room, and it will never open for you. Give it back to us: the abbey pays the finder's share, and blesses your door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:252
msgid "The saint's chest is gone. Somewhere a Keywright will try to open it, and it won't, and they'll never know why. Pray for whoever has it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:257
#, csharp-format
msgid "Give it back (+{0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:263
msgid "You gave the reliquary back to the abbey."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:264
msgid "Bless you. The saint will remember, and so will we."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:266 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1368 scripts/Phases/CounterPhase.cs:517
#: scripts/Phases/DayEndPhase.cs:395 scripts/Ui/SongReveal.cs:174
msgid "Keep it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:269
msgid "Then may it sit in the dark with you, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:286
msgid "\"Keywright. The abbey's chest was my runner's mistake, and Flick has been told. I take back what the Guild took from families who couldn't pay its tithe, and I give it back to them. Leave me be, and I'll remember it. M.\" A black feather falls out of the letter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:291
msgid "Burn it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:294
msgid "The feather curls up in the grate. Somewhere, somebody knows."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:296
msgid "Show it to Hollis"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:300
msgid "Hollis turns the feather over. \"Her calling card. She's close, then.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:307
#, csharp-format
msgid "Three more thefts this week, every one a chest the Guild had foreclosed on. A carter saw the thief: {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:311
msgid "The carter's word"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:311 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:312
#, csharp-format
msgid "A carter saw the Magpie: {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:318
#, csharp-format
msgid "Wardens say a goblin did the abbey! Nettle's cousin saw the thief on the burrow road: {0}. Not a goblin! Tell the sergeant."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:322
msgid "A goblin's word"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:322
#, csharp-format
msgid "Nettle's cousin saw the Magpie on the burrow road: {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:323
#, csharp-format
msgid "Nettle's cousin saw the Magpie: {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:330
#, csharp-format
msgid "The Magpie's bounty is up to {0}. We've three names: Bettany Crane at the Crossed Keys, Aunt Hesper the matchmaker, and Rook Varga, who's hunting the bounty herself."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:332
msgid "You've heard what the carter saw, and the goblin. You've met all three. Who is it?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:336
msgid "I won't name anyone"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:340
msgid "You wouldn't name anyone for the Magpie's bounty."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:341
msgid "Have it your way. The bounty stands, if you change your mind."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:348
msgid "\"You sent an innocent woman to the Wardens' cells, Keywright. I'll get her out. And thank you for the diversion: it kept the Wardens busy all week. M.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:357
msgid "A knock at the back door. A hooded woman: she lowers her hood, and smiles."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:358
msgid "You didn't give them my name, Keywright. I'm grateful, and the Lockless pay their debts. Take this: from a Guild strongroom, so it's nobody's now but yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:365
#, csharp-format
msgid "The Magpie came to the back door: {0}. She left you {1}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:374
msgid "The Marked Child"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:375
msgid "Pip Hollow, the washerwoman's boy, has the Key-mark on his palm. The Guild's Mark-Finders take marked children into its counting-houses, and they're testing hands at the fair."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:383
msgid "Mister? My hand's been itching ever since I fished up that last chest. Look: there's a mark on it. Like a key. Like yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:387
msgid "Tell him what it means"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:390
msgid "Pip has the Key-mark, and you told him what it means."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:391
msgid "A Keywright? Me? Mum'll faint."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:393
msgid "Tell him to keep it hidden"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:395
msgid "Pip has the Key-mark. You told him to keep his hand in his pocket."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:396
msgid "In my pocket. Got it. Is it a bad thing, mister?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:404
msgid "Mistress Aubel, Mark-Finder for the Gilded Guild. We test the children's hands at the fair tomorrow. The Guild takes the marked ones into its care: they want for nothing, all their lives."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:406
#, csharp-format
msgid "A Keywright knows the itch when it starts. If you know of a marked child, a name is worth {0} to the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:409
msgid "Pip Hollow, the millpond boy"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:417
msgid "You gave the Mark-Finder Pip's name. The Guild took him into its care, and Wynn left Brindle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:418
msgid "The Guild thanks you. He'll be well looked after. And the Guild remembers its friends: its bailiff calls on them first."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:420
msgid "None that I know of"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:422
msgid "You told the Mark-Finder you knew of no marked child."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:423
msgid "Hm. The fair will tell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:431
msgid "I'm Pip's mum. The Guild's men are going door to door, looking at children's hands. He told me what you are."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:432
msgid "Will you hide him? He'd sleep in your back room and work for his keep, and he's a good boy. Please."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:435
msgid "He can stay, as my apprentice"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:439
msgid "You took Pip on as your apprentice, and hid him in the back room."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:440
msgid "Bless you. Oh, bless you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:442
msgid "I can't risk it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:447
msgid "You wouldn't hide Pip. The Guild found him at the fair."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:448
msgid "Then they'll find him. They always do."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:455
msgid "A knock after dark. \"Mistress Aubel. Open up, Keywright. We're told there's a marked child under your roof.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:460
msgid "There's no child here"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:464
msgid "You turned the Mark-Finder away. Pip's your apprentice now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:465
msgid "We'll see. The Guild is patient, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:467
msgid "Take him"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:473
msgid "You let the Mark-Finder take Pip."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:474
msgid "A wise choice."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:478
msgid "The Guild still takes Bram's word"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:482
msgid "Bram gave his word for you, and the Mark-Finder went away. Pip's your apprentice now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:483
msgid "Bram's word. Very well. The Guild will remember it was spent on this."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:493
msgid "Pip says you stood in the door and told the Guild there was no child here. The whole mill knows it, and half of Brindle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:494
msgid "We haven't the coin to thank you. But we've neighbours, and every one of them will sell to you at a neighbour's price while my boy's safe with you: a sixth off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:498
msgid "Thank your neighbours for me"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:502
msgid "Brindle's regulars sell to you at a neighbour's price now, a sixth off, while Pip's safe with you. Wynn owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:503
msgid "And if the Guild ever comes for more than its due, send for me. The whole mill will come."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:505
msgid "Keep your neighbours' coin"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:509
msgid "You wouldn't take a neighbour's price for hiding Pip. Brindle hasn't stopped talking about it. Wynn owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:510
msgid "Then I'll tell everyone that too. And if the Guild comes for more than its due, send for me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:518
msgid "Master, the Mark-Finder was at the Thornwick fair. She keeps a book: every marked child's name, and where the Guild sent them. Some of them were six."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:520
msgid "She leaves it on her table while she eats her pie. I could copy a page. I'm quick, and I'm small."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:523
msgid "Copy one page, and run"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:527
msgid "Pip copied a page of the Mark-Finder's register: children the Guild took, and where it sent them. A paper for the case against the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:528
msgid "Done before she'd finished her crust! Forty names. I knew two of them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:530
msgid "Too dangerous. Stay here"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:532
msgid "You wouldn't let Pip near the Mark-Finder's register."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:533
msgid "Yes, master. I'll sweep, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:543
msgid "The Widow's Debt"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:544
msgid "Ada Kettle's son Jory is in the Guild's debt-house for his dead father's tithe. Her husband Rafe's sword, with KETTLE on the blade, was pawned years ago in Crownhold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:553
msgid "My boy Jory's in the Guild's debt-house in Crownhold, for his father's tithe: the Guild says Rafe owed it. Two years he's been in there."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:555
msgid "And if you ever find Rafe's sword in a chest, dear, KETTLE on the blade... it was pawned when he died. I'd give anything to have it back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:559
msgid "Ada Kettle seeks her husband's sword"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:560
msgid "A soldier's sword with KETTLE on the blade, pawned in Crownhold years ago. Ada Kettle, at Brindle, would give anything for it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:561
msgid "Ada's son Jory is in the Guild's debt-house. Her husband Rafe's sword was pawned in Crownhold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:571
msgid "A soldier's pledge, never redeemed. The ticket says \"Kettle: one sword, and sundries\". {articles} in all, it says. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:583
msgid "You bought Silas Brass's pledge with Rafe Kettle's sword in it. Bram set the sword aside for Ada."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:585
msgid "You passed on Silas Brass's pledge with Rafe Kettle's sword in it. Someone else will have it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:590
msgid "I came up to Crownhold to see Jory, and Bram sent word: you found Rafe's sword! Oh, dear. May I see it?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:593
msgid "It's yours"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:599
msgid "You gave Ada her husband's sword, and she gave you his medal to keep. She owes you a favour, she says, and she means it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:600
msgid "Rafe's sword. Oh, Rafe. Here: his medal, from two wars. He'd want it with someone kind. Thank you, dear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:602
#, csharp-format
msgid "Sell it to her for what she has ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:606
msgid "You sold Ada her husband's sword for what she had."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:607
msgid "It's all I have, but it's his. Thank you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:609
#, csharp-format
msgid "Sell it on ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:613
msgid "You sold Rafe Kettle's sword on."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:614
msgid "Oh. Of course. It's yours to sell, I suppose."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:620
msgid "Ada, about Jory"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:621
#, csharp-format
msgid "The debt-house wants {0} for Jory, and I've saved half of it. If you could find the rest... he's a strong lad, and he'd work for you till it was paid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:625 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:656
#, csharp-format
msgid "Pay the rest ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:630
msgid "You paid the rest of Jory's debt. He'll carry chests in for you for a week, to pay you back: one more customer a day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:631
msgid "Jory's free! He'll work a week for you to pay you back, dear. He'll carry anything."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:633 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:665 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:771
msgid "I can't"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:637
msgid "You couldn't pay Jory's debt. The Guild has called his note in, on its next night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:638
msgid "I understand, dear. I'll keep saving. They say they'll collect him if it's not paid. Collect. Like a parcel."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:646
msgid "Ada, about Jory's note"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:649
msgid "The Guild's posted Jory's note on the debt-house door, dear. It falls due on the Guild's night. Old Haddon's went the same way, and nobody's seen him since."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:651
msgid "The Guild's posted Jory's note on the debt-house door, dear. It falls due on the Guild's night. That's how they take people: a note on a door, and a cart on the Guild's night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:653
#, csharp-format
msgid "I've still half of it. {0} more and he's free. Please."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:662
msgid "You paid Jory's note the week the Guild called it in. He'll carry chests in for you for a week: one more customer a day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:663
msgid "Jory's free! Oh, dear. He'll work a week for you, and carry anything."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:667
msgid "You couldn't pay Jory's note before the Guild's night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:668
msgid "Then I'll sit with him tonight. Whatever they do, he won't be alone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:676
msgid "Ada at the back door in her shawl, shaking. \"They came for Jory with a cart, dear. To work off the note, they said. They wouldn't say where.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:678
msgid "\"I don't care what they say he owes. He's my boy.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:679
msgid "The Guild collected Jory Kettle on its night, with a cart, to work off his note. Nobody will say where they took him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:686
msgid "Two years I scrubbed the debt-house floors, and the clerks never minded me reading over their shoulders. Half the debts in there were never owed: the Guild adds a tithe to a dead man's name and sends for his son."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:688
msgid "I can write down what I saw, names and sums. Would it help anyone?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:691
msgid "Write it all down"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:695
msgid "Jory wrote down the debt-house's tallies: debts the Guild made up. A paper for the case against the Guild. He owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:696
msgid "Every name I can remember. And I don't forget a sum."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:698
msgid "Put it behind you, Jory"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:701
msgid "Jory put the debt-house behind him. He owes you a favour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:702
msgid "Maybe you're right. I'll carry chests and forget it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:712
msgid "The Deep Door"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:713
msgid "Tobin the adventurer has found a door at the bottom of the Barrow, sealed with the Key-mark and untouched since the Locking. He needs a Keywright's stake to go through it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:722
msgid "There's a door at the bottom of the Barrow, Keywright: stone, with a keyhole shaped like your mark. Nobody's been through it since the Locking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:724
#, csharp-format
msgid "Stake me {0} for rope, lamps and two good men, and half of what's behind it is yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:727
#, csharp-format
msgid "Here's the money ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:731
msgid "Tobin, back from the Barrow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:732
msgid "You staked Tobin to go through the Barrow's deep door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:733
msgid "You won't regret it. Four days, and I'll be back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:735
msgid "Not this time"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:735
msgid "Someone at the Crossed Keys will stake me, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:747
msgid "Behind the door: a vault nobody had touched since the Locking. Half's yours, like I said: this one, freely given. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:750
msgid "Tobin came back from the deep door with a hoard, and gave you your half."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:751
msgid "Tobin came back from the deep door with a hoard. You wouldn't take your half."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:758
msgid "Tobin's men came back to the Crossed Keys without him. He's alive: they heard him calling, under a fallen arch past the door."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:760
#, csharp-format
msgid "A rescue wants a crew from Crownhold, and that's {0}. Nobody here has it, love."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:763
#, csharp-format
msgid "Pay for the rescue ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:767
msgid "Tobin, rescued"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:768
msgid "Tobin was trapped past the deep door. You paid for his rescue."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:769
msgid "I'll send for the crew tonight. Bless you, love."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:776
msgid "Tobin was trapped past the deep door, and there was no rescue."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:777
msgid "Then I'll light a candle for him at the Crossed Keys."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:789
msgid "You came for me. Half of what's behind that door is yours, freely given, and I'm never going down again. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:796
msgid "Tobin came back alive, and gave you half of what was behind the door. He owes you his life, he says."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:806
msgid "I swore I'd never go down again. But I keep dreaming of what I saw past the arch that fell on me: a stair, going down, and light at the bottom of it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:808
msgid "Behind the vault there's a stair. It goes down further than the Barrow should go, and there's light at the bottom, and water, and bells."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:809
#, csharp-format
msgid "The old kings' halls, I reckon: the ones the songs say the Barrow was built over. Stake me {0}, a proper crew this time, and half of whatever's down there is yours, every week I'm digging."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:813
#, csharp-format
msgid "Stake the expedition ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:817
msgid "Tobin, back from under the Barrow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:818
msgid "Past the deep door there's a stair down to the old kings' halls. You staked Tobin's expedition."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:819
msgid "Four days. If I'm not back in six, don't send anyone. I mean it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:821
msgid "Once was enough"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:823
msgid "Tobin found a stair down to the old kings' halls. You told him once was enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:824
msgid "You're right. You're right. I'll stop dreaming about it. Probably."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:836
msgid "Halls, Keywright, halls under halls, and the kings asleep in them with their crowns on. Your half: freely given. One coin, for luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:839
msgid "Tobin came back from the old kings' halls under the Barrow, and gave you your half."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:840
msgid "Tobin came back from the old kings' halls under the Barrow. You wouldn't take your half."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:846
msgid "I'm going back down, and I'm staying: there are years of halls down there. Here, my lamp. Hang it in your window."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:847
msgid "Every week, first thing, I'll send up a chest for you, given freely, the way it should be. The lamp's how my lads will find you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:851
msgid "Tobin is digging under the Barrow for good. He gave you his lamp: a chest from him every week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:860
msgid "The Woodcutters"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:861
msgid "The Guild is buying the felling rights on the Old Wood, and its deed wants a Keywright's mark as witness. The druids and the fair folk who live there want a promise instead."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:870
msgid "Harl Caskett, timber factor for the Gilded Guild. The Guild's buying the felling rights on the Old Wood. The druids won't sign, so the deed wants a licensed Keywright's mark as witness."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:872
#, csharp-format
msgid "Put your mark to it, and the Guild pays a witness's fee: {0}, a tenth of your next due."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:875 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:933
msgid "Seal it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:882
msgid "You put your mark to the Guild's deed for the Old Wood. The witness copy names the coin it was paid in: seized from families."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:883
msgid "A pleasure. The axes go in at the full moon."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:885 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:956 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1189
msgid "Refuse"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:890
msgid "You wouldn't put your mark to the Guild's deed for the Old Wood."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:891
msgid "The Guild will find another Keywright. It always does."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:899
msgid "You put your mark to Caskett's deed, child. The axes come at the full moon, and the Wood will remember whose mark it was."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:901
msgid "You wouldn't put your mark to Caskett's deed. The Hawthorn Lady has heard of it, and she would speak with you. Leave your back door unlatched tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:908
msgid "The door opens on its own, and the shop smells of hawthorn. \"Keywright. The Guild will find another mark for its deed, unless the one who refused it keeps refusing.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:910
msgid "\"Promise me you'll keep the Wood's oaks standing, and have this: a charm the Wood has kept since before the Locking. A promise to us is kept, or paid for.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:914
msgid "I promise"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:920
msgid "You promised the Hawthorn Lady to keep the Wood's oaks standing. She gave you the Hawthorn Charm."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:921
msgid "\"Kept, or paid for.\" She leaves a sprig of hawthorn, bound in silver, on the counter, and is gone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:923
msgid "\"Then we'll speak no more of it.\" The hawthorn smell is gone by morning."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:929
#, csharp-format
msgid "Last time, Keywright. The Guild will pay a fifth of your next due for your mark on the Wood's deed: {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:942
msgid " A promise broken: the Hawthorn Charm has crumbled to dry leaves."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:948
msgid " A promise broken: the Hawthorn Lady's charm is gone from your case."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:953
msgid "You sealed the Guild's deed for the Old Wood after all. Mother Sorrel won't trade with you again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:954
msgid "Sensible. The axes go in tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:961
msgid "You refused the Guild's deed for the Old Wood a second time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:962
msgid "Then the Guild will remember it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:969
msgid "Hawthorn again, and a voice from nowhere: \"Twice you refused them. The Wood keeps its own.\" Something is left on the counter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:974
#, csharp-format
msgid "The Hawthorn Lady thanked you with {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:983
msgid "The Parcel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:984
msgid "Corvin Tallow the smuggler needs somewhere to keep a parcel for two nights, no questions asked, and the Wardens are searching the market."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:992
#, csharp-format
msgid "A favour, Keywright. Keep this parcel in your back room two nights. Don't open it: it isn't yours, so it wouldn't anyway. {0} when I collect."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:996
msgid "Deal"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1000
msgid "You're keeping Corvin's parcel in your back room."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1001
msgid "Good. Two nights. Nobody needs to know."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1003 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1433 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1442
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1003
msgid "Pity. Forget I asked."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1010
msgid "Hollis at the door, after dark. \"We're searching every back room on the market tonight. Not yours: I told the lads you're a friend of the Wardens. Good night, Keywright.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1012
msgid "Hollis at the door, after dark. \"Wardens. We're searching every back room on the market tonight.\" He comes out with Corvin's parcel. \"And what's this?\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1016
msgid "It's Corvin Tallow's"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1023
msgid "The Wardens found Corvin's parcel, and you told them whose it was. Corvin's gone from the market."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1024
msgid "Contraband brandy, and a chest off the Guild's foreclosure list. Thank you, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1026
msgid "It's mine"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1033
msgid "The Wardens found Corvin's parcel. You said it was yours, and paid the fine."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1034
#, csharp-format
msgid "Contraband, Keywright. That's a fine of {0}, and it's confiscated."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1040
msgid "Corvin, for his parcel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1042
#, csharp-format
msgid "My parcel, safe and sound. You're a friend, Keywright. Here's {0}, and something from my own pocket."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1050
#, csharp-format
msgid "Corvin collected his parcel: he paid, and gave you {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1059
msgid "The Foreclosures"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1060
msgid "Half the chests the Guild forecloses on won't open for any Keywright it sells them to. A clerk in its counting-house wants to know why, and the answer is in the Chest Roll."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1069
msgid "Tobias Fenn, clerk at the Guild's counting-house. Forgive me: I've a question I can't ask at work."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1070
msgid "Half the chests the Guild forecloses on won't open for any Keywright it sells them to. The ledgers say they're sent \"below\", unopened. Why won't they open?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1074
msgid "Seizure isn't a sale: they're still the families'"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1077
msgid "Tobias Fenn asked why the Guild's foreclosed chests won't open. You told him: they're still the families'."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1078
msgid "Then the Guild's been selling stolen chests. For a hundred years. Oh dear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1080
msgid "Ask the Guild"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1082
msgid "Tobias Fenn asked why the Guild's foreclosed chests won't open. You sent him back to the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1083
msgid "I... yes. Of course. Forget I asked."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1091
msgid "The Guild took my family's hall and sold its chests. I bought grandfather's war chest back, and it's mine to sell: it won't open for their Keywright. The sword's mine, for {fee}. The rest: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1093
msgid "Sir Rowan sold you his grandfather's war chest, bought back from the Guild: it was his, so it opened for you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1099
msgid "Master Quire, the Royal Archivist. Your clerk friend came to me. The Chest Roll agrees with you: every chest the Guild has seized is still in the families' names."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1101
msgid "By the ward's own law the Guild has been selling stolen chests for a century, and sending the ones that won't open down through the Gate. I've made you a copy of the Roll."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1110
msgid "I'll take it to the King"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1115
msgid "Master Quire gave you a copy of the Chest Roll. You'll take it to the King."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1116
msgid "The King. Yes. If anyone can make the Guild answer for it, he can."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1118
#, csharp-format
msgid "Sell the copy to the Guild ({0}g)"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1124
msgid "You sold the copy of the Chest Roll to the Guild. Tobias Fenn hasn't been seen since."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1125
msgid "You'd... very well. It's yours to sell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1133
msgid "Tobias at the back door, with a travelling bag. \"They know I talked. I'm leaving Crownhold tonight. Take this: a page from the Guild's own ledgers. Every tithe, and where it goes. 'Below.'\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1135
msgid " Jory Kettle's with him: \"I'll swear to the King what the debt-house is full of.\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1143
msgid "Tobias Fenn left Crownhold, and left you a page of the Guild's ledgers: where the tithe goes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1148
msgid "The King, for the Roll"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1150
msgid "You've something for the Crown, I hear. The Roll, and a page of the Guild's own ledgers. Let me see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1151
msgid "The Guild's been robbing my subjects in my name, and sending it to the Maw. My decree: the Guild's tithe on Keywrights is cut by a fifth, from tonight. Vane will be... displeased."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1159
msgid "The King cut the Guild's tithe by a fifth. The Guild will remember who brought him the Roll."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1168
msgid "The Unlocking"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1169
msgid "Archmage Orme of the Arcanum is building an engine to copy the Key-mark, so that any chest would open for anyone. She needs a Keywright's blood, and Mara says it would end the Locking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1177
#, csharp-format
msgid "My mistress, Archmage Orme, asks a favour: one drop of a Keywright's blood, on a brass plate. That's all. She'll pay {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1181
msgid "Give it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1186
msgid "You gave Archmage Orme a drop of your blood on a brass plate."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1187
msgid "Thank you! She'll be so pleased. I think."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1192
msgid "You wouldn't give Archmage Orme your blood."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1193
msgid "Oh. She'll find someone else. She always does."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1199
msgid "Ilse, worried"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1202
msgid "Your blood's in her engine. She's building something to copy the mark: with it, any chest would open for anyone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1203
msgid "She found another Keywright's blood. She's building an engine to copy the mark: any chest would open for anyone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1204
msgid "Mara came to the Arcanum last night. She says if the mark can be copied, the Locking's finished, and the realm with it. I don't know what to do."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1208
msgid "Help her break it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1215
#, csharp-format
msgid "You helped Ilse break Orme's engine. She gave you {0} from the Arcanum's stores."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1216
#, csharp-format
msgid "Then I'll do it tonight. Take this, from the stores: {0}. She'll never miss it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1218
msgid "Tell the Guild"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1224
msgid "You told the Guild about Orme's engine. They took her away, and paid you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1225
msgid "The Guild? Oh no. Oh, no."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1227
msgid "Stay out of it"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1230
msgid "You stayed out of Orme's engine."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1231
msgid "I... all right. I'll stay out of it too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1239
msgid "It works, Keywright. Partly: one chest in three opens for anyone at all. The Guild has offered me the moon for it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1240
#, csharp-format
msgid "And the Gate is cracking: the Maw's gilded iron is leaking into every purse in the realm. Here: {0}, your share, for the blood."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1245
msgid "Orme's engine works, partly, and the Gate is cracking: demon gold is everywhere now, in any purse of coin."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1254
msgid "Ironroot's Crown"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1255
msgid "Ironroot's crown was locked in the Royal Treasury at the Locking, and the Guild bans dwarf-gold. Durgan Ironhand wants it home under the mountain, and only the King can give it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1264
msgid "At the Locking, the King's men locked Ironroot's crown in the Royal Treasury with everything else. Three hundred years it's sat there."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1266
msgid "The Guild calls our gold contraband because we won't pay its tithe. If the crown came home, every dwarf in Ironroot would remember who brought it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1270
msgid "I'll ask the King"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1274
msgid "You told Durgan you'd ask the King for Ironroot's crown."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1275
msgid "Ha! A surface-dweller with a spine. We'll see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1277
msgid "Nothing I can do"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1277
msgid "Hmph. Nobody ever can."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1288
msgid "Ironroot's crown? It's in a chest I can't open, like everything I own. Here: I give it to you. Keep what else is in it, and give the dwarves their crown."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1296
msgid "The King gave you the chest with Ironroot's crown in it. Bram set the crown aside for the dwarves."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1302
msgid "The crown! Ironroot owes you a debt it won't forget, Keywright. Our smiths will build you what you need, for nothing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1312
#, csharp-format
msgid "Ironroot's smiths built you a {0}, for nothing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1312
msgid "Ironroot paid you for the crown in dwarf-gold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1321
msgid "The Vell Inheritance"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1322
msgid "Lord Cassian Vell is selling his sister's chests to pay his debts, and they aren't his to sell: their grandmother's will left them to Lady Isaura. A chest sold by the wrong hands is cold to the mark."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1335
msgid "Grandmother's trick box. I need it gone before the tables open tonight: {price}, and not a word to my sister."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1338
msgid "You bought a trick box from Lord Cassian. It won't open: it's his sister's."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1343
msgid "Lord Cassian tried to sell you his sister's trick box. You sent for the Wardens."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1344
msgid "Lord Cassian tried to sell you his sister's trick box. You passed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1351
msgid "My brother sold you grandmother's box. It's mine, by her will, so it won't open for you. Give it back to me, and I'll give it to you properly. Then it will."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1354
msgid "Cassian spent a night in the Wardens' cells over grandmother's box. It did him good. Thank you, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1355
msgid "Cassian sold one of grandmother's boxes to someone. It will never open for them, and he knows it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1359
msgid "Give it back"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1365
msgid "You gave Lady Isaura her grandmother's box back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1366
msgid "Thank you. I'll bring it back tomorrow: freely given, it'll open for you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1371
msgid "You kept Lady Isaura's box."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1372
msgid "Then it sits in your back room forever. How very Vell of you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1384
msgid "Isaura, with grandmother's box"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1386
msgid "Grandmother's box, freely given. Now it's yours, and it will open. One coin, for luck: she'd have insisted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1387
msgid "Lady Isaura gave you grandmother's box, and it opened."
